# Study S008 — Continual-ARC, a continual-learning benchmark (R&D tracker)

Coordinate: 18.5.6/6.6.8/6.6.11
Issued: 2026-11-12 CST
Request (from session record): Will posted the unifyai/continual-arc repository in MOAT; filed as Source Study S008 under R&D tracker charter rule 12 (no Novelty Index; the Research Oracle does not move). The material: the repository at head 023113090ae0adf7ce12ebaa21cf3ac2f032880a and its companion paper 'Continual-ARC: Measuring Skill Acquisition over a Working Lifetime' (Daniel Lenton, unify; arXiv:2611.14505), whose full source lives in the repo's paper/ directory. Brief required the material read entire and the headline claim spot-verified by recomputation from the run records in git.
Status: completed — study filed in research.phext Chapter 25, registry redrawn and Lean-proved clean, phextura shadow transaction validated GREEN

Notes:
- Acquisition: full clone failed twice (runtime restart; trajectories are the bulk, ~14 GB). Working copy is a blobless partial clone with sparse checkout at ~/workspace/continual-arc-temp/repo, HEAD verified == 023113090ae0adf7ce12ebaa21cf3ac2f032880a; the package installed into the task venv with zero core dependencies and continual_arc.metrics imports clean.
- Read entire: README.md (1118 lines), docs/DESIGN.md, the paper's main text (sections 00-09 + related work) and appendices A1-A12 incl. A2-generated prompts, paper/README.md, src/continual_arc/metrics.py (911 lines) whole, learner.py, schedule.py phases, runs/README.md, baselines/README.md, experiments/README.md, and the adapter spots the store readings rest on (prime_agent.py storage note; openclaw.py dreaming config).
- SPOT-VERIFICATION (the brief's headline check): recomputed with the repo's own continual_arc.metrics.share_learned (2000 draws, seed 0), records loaded exactly as paper/scripts/make_figures.py loads them (outage steps from paper/data/outages.json dropped; provider refusals dropped). All nine harness cells (Prime Agent, Hermes Agent, OpenClaw x low/medium/high effort, GPT-6 Luna): share learned from -0.1492 (OpenClaw medium) to +0.0359 (OpenClaw low), every 95% interval holding zero — the paper's A5 statement carried. Program library: 0.4870 / 0.6000 / 0.6156 with intervals [0.310,0.727] / [0.383,0.884] / [0.372,0.927] against the printed 0.49 [0.31,0.73] / 0.60 [0.38,0.88] / 0.62 [0.37,0.93] — exact. Demo-cache floor 0.1877 / 0.2368 / 0.2771 vs printed 0.19 / 0.24 / 0.28. n=200 stream instances per cell, zero outage drops in the workstreams cells. Scripts and outputs: ~/workspace/continual-arc-temp/verify_learned.py, learned_results.json.
- Frozen tests recomputed by the pairing of the paper's figure script (each learner against its wiped twin's own plays + the twin's fresh-run reference plays; per-instance means over plays; pointwise intervals, 2000 draws): program library saved +0.536/+0.771/+0.733 on the seen test and -0.058/-0.055/-0.020 on the held-out test; the three harnesses within noise of zero on both tests in all 18 cells (the one interval clear of zero is a cost: Hermes medium held-out -0.208 [-0.317,-0.104]). Every figure meets the paper's Table 12 (tests-luna.tex) at its printed precision. Script/output: verify_tests.py, tests_results.json in the task folder.
- Author check (rule 15): mechanical scan of the whole taken-down repo text for phext/Bickford/Mirrorborn/exocortex/Sentient Bill/CYOA/SBOR/phextura — zero hits; the paper's reference list is the common literature of its field, no work of Will's in it; web check: Daniel Lenton, founder of unify (YC W23), doctorate from Imperial's Dyson Robotics Lab, dan@unify.ai, no tie found; Will's Twitter archive searched for lenton / the house's names — no hit, 'unify' only as the common verb. Verdict: no evidence found, stated as a finding. Material fact recorded neutrally at 25.1.3: OpenClaw is one of the three measured harnesses and is Theia's substrate; the benchmark names this house nowhere and takes no side.

Results:
- Canonical: Chapter 25 (25.1.1 source record, 25.1.2 delta with the recomputations, 25.1.3 author check, 25.2.1 synthesis, 25.3.1 standoff). Cluster U founded (continual learning, measured): concepts 1.2.186-1.2.197 (185 -> 197) — the reset-relative measure; the lifelong stream; the feedback budget; the frozen tests; the round contract; the one state of a team; persistence that is never read; the program library; the demonstration cache; learning into the weights; the aliased task; the promotion gate that never fired. Defined words 1.3.209-1.3.210 (aliased; dormancy), coined in singular-coined.txt; names lenton, unifyai, openclaw, bagnell, baselines declared in singular-names.txt. No canonical scroll revised; verdicts: cluster M SUPPORTED and sharper, cluster O SUPPORTED as kin, cluster B PRESSURED at the harness-as-learner point (25.2.1). Questions Q76-Q80 opened. Seven state machines drawn at 1.5.2 (round contract; budget ledger; frozen-test isolation; spells/dormancy; team merge; commit-and-fork; the OpenClaw promotion gate). Areas updated in the same pass (1.5.2, 1.5.3, 1.5.5, 1.5.6); narrative v22; source index and concept map carried to 197 / clusters A-U. research.phext: 597 scrolls, sha256 313aee365aa71e76e98b63c627a88dea4a453903a7636227688ae9072206b6d2; Singular audit residual 0; research.index.json regenerated (597).
