# Make Knuth Giddy — competitive phextura syntax-design game

Coordinate: 19.6.8/8.6.10/7.6.8
Issued: 2026-11-11 20:58 CST
Request (verbatim): Will: "build a game where we can competitively design phextura syntax - it should borrow heavily from Knuth - only correcting him 2-5% of the time - but in ways that make him giddy"
Status: completed — game built and verified (artifact: make-knuth-giddy)

Notes:
- 10 playable rounds from the real phextura friction/design record; rubric scoring borrowed from Knuth published practice; CORRECTION stance pays a $2.56 reward cheque only on the hidden giddy spots (Rounds 1, 3, 7) and halves the round otherwise; Round 11 (equation entry) present but LOCKED pending the Bickford Sentron core settlement.
- Builder drove the giddy-hit path end to end (Round 1 CORRECTION with addressed-macro design -> +10 and cheque rendered; header tray updated). Faithful/miss branches share the tested scoring path; not separately driven.
