# Ranch node Tailworm audit (Tailscale TS-2026-014 to TS-2026-017)

Coordinate: 22.8.12/10.8.15/5.6.7
Issued: 2026-11-10 20:10 CST
Request (verbatim): Audit your ranch nodes for Tailworm exposure - Let's do it!
Status: complete - report delivered 2026-11-10 20:15 CST; no upgrades applied (read-only audit)

Notes:
- Judged only against Tailscale 1.104.4 and bulletins TS-2026-014..017 (Cyberdione Labs Tailworm report, 2026-10-25; fixes shipped in 1.104.4 on 2026-10-28).
- 14 nodes assessed live: all on Tailscale 1.104.5, Tailscale SSH off everywhere (fleet uses OpenSSH over the tailnet - not a Tailworm surface); Serve present only on Quacked Hill and Elven Path, both tailnet-only on the patched client. No exposed nodes; staged upgrade commands in the report, none run.
- 11 devices unassessed (never cleared): 7 online but outside the ranch access configuration (kaleidoscope-one, yeet-max, jacked-kite, great-white, moon-beam, west-lincoln, uncanny-valley - peer data shows no TS SSH keys and no Serve services advertised); 4 offline (aurora-continuum, delta-wood, best-willow, splinter).
- Access lesson: fleet-ssh.sh's known_hosts on this VM lacks most nodes; the ranch-proxy (~/workspace/ranch-proxy, daemon-owned known_hosts) reached every configured node cleanly.

Results:
- Report: ~/workspace/tailworm-audit-task/AUDIT.md and the delivered document in ~/workspace/your_files/ranch-node-tailworm-audit/ (byte-identical). Inscribed in artifacts.phext at 30.6.8/7.6.10/7.5.9.
# Install an indexed search (exo-search)

Coordinate: 23.5.10/7.6.11/8.5.7
Issued: 2026-11-11 01:27 CST
Request (verbatim): you need to install an indexed search - whatever you're doing to search sucks
Status: complete — exo-search built, validated, published

Notes:
- Will's correction after the Twitter-wishes pass: per-question bespoke scripts re-scanning the 53MB tweets.json missed whole classes (the Dear #Internet address form).
- Built ~/workspace/tools/exo-search: SQLite FTS5 (unicode61), one persistent index ~/workspace/search-index/exo.db (45MB) over tweets 29,539 + memory chunks 4,937 + phext scrolls 3,306 = 37,782 docs; build 5.1s; BM25 query/phrase/NEAR, --source/--after/--before filters, count census mode.
- Validation: term censuses vs brute force — phext 1028, exocortex 684, wish 84, internet 416, dunbar 10, telepathy 8, kardashev 45 — 7/7 identical; phrase 'dear internet' 44=44. Published to wbic16/emise-tools@exo tools/exo-search (mode carried from local exec bit), remote bytes verified identical.

Results:
- exo-search is the standing search route for the corpus; rebuild with 'exo-search build' after corpus changes.
# Enable the phextnet: deploy qexo v1.2.0 to the 19 keyed nodes, cross-register all peers, name aletheia-core release signer, serve live fleet-wide

Coordinate: 23.6.7/7.8.12/10.5.7
Issued: 2026-11-13 00:29 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-13 00:29 CST) after merging PR #15: 'build/deploy and I'll attempt to test from my laptop'. Build v1.2.0 from exo 833e2f34 (Linux + Windows-gnu qexo.exe for Will's laptop), roll the binary to the 19 keyed nodes, cross-register every peer with its tailnet endpoint on every node, set release_signer = aletheia-core's fingerprint fleet-wide, serve_bind = each node's tailnet address with qexo serve running as a service, aletheia-core publishes the signed v1.2.0 release, and prove the phextnet end-to-end from at least two nodes (list shows peers; update --check reads already-current through the real network path; evolve --check plans without writing).
Status: DEPLOYED 2026-11-13: qexo v1.2.0 (exo 833e2f34) built on aletheia-core (linux sha256 e44c8dab…, windows exe 39e897c4… at fleet-keys/qexo-v1.2.0.exe) and deployed to all 19 keyed nodes — binary hash-verified per node, doctor exit 0, config serve_bind=<own tailnet IP> + release_signer=aletheia-core (A4E7277F…) on every node, 18 peers cross-registered with :8484 endpoints per node, qexo-serve.service active fleet-wide, signer announced the 1.2.0 release (manifest 6.6.6/8.1.1/1.1.1). End-to-end proof from yeet-max over the real tailnet: update --check → 'already current — the trusted signer offers 1.2.0', evolve --check byte-inert, 306 gossip confirmations. Timers left OFF (auto_update/evolve) pending Will's laptop tests. Signer-local note: aletheia-core's own update refuses by design (its key is not in its own registry). Record: fleet-keys/ROLLOUT-RECORD.md DEPLOY addendum.

Results:
- 2026-11-13: phextnet live on 19 nodes; proof transcripts in ~/workspace/qexo-task/enable/results/proof-*.txt
# Paper 017 — ingest 'AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal's Security at the Machine-Code Level' (Google DeepMind document 36) into the R&D tracker (Chapter 27)

Coordinate: 23.6.8/7.6.13/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-13
Request (verbatim): https://deepmind.google/documents/36/Formal_Verification_of_Signal_4.pdf
Status: complete — ingested, scored, proved, shadow-synced and journalled in one pass, 2026-11-13

Notes:
- 2026-11-13 01:24 CST: Will posted the paper in MOAT with the instruction 'ingest and update research.phext and research.phextura'. Not an arXiv paper — a Google DeepMind document (dated 2026-11-10) — so the blind skim's basis was the title + abstract on the PDF's own first page, read from page 1 only. Protocol order held: BEFORE prediction sealed in thirst-quest predictions.jsonl, commit 31566b7, BEFORE the full text was downloaded.
- Seal: 11 new, 1 revised (at 1.2.48), no axis, NI 0.0532, 17 links (11/6), 3 questions, Oracle to 80% (70–90) up. Actual: 17 new (MISS +6 — testing a specification, the amendment protocol, the concretization gamma bound, the collision clause, priced reductions, and joint assumptions each stood separately), 1 revised (count and target exact), no axis (exact — 10/10 calls, first scored no-axis call), NI 0.0788 (|error| 0.0256, largest since P012; rolling mean 0.0166 at n=10), links 41 (36 inside / 5 across), questions 4 (Q85–Q88), Oracle 80% (70–90) — point and range exact, fifth paper running.
- Chapter 27; cluster W (the verified artifact) founded at 1.2.206–1.2.222; foundations 1.3.212–1.3.213; defined words 1.3.214–1.3.218 (5 words, 6 forms). Rider on 1.2.48: translation-verification is one of two poles. Restructure Pass #11 executed (220 trigger crossed at 222): merges none; Q/W and S/W seams held on evidence. Seven state machines drawn in Ch.27 (5 stated, 2 inferred); tracker totals 78. Author check #18: no evidence found.
- Registry 644 entries (True 296 = 258 stipulation + 38 verified / Unknown 348 = 302 attributed + 27 synthesis + 17 open + 2 estimate / False 0 / Fiction 0), drawn at a verified fixed point (two extractions byte-identical) over research.phext sha256 329e623b8853774c762660aa57de782f3c08e9412d92d2a6999392e83bf87488; Lean proof clean in ~/research-tracker-epistemic-p017 and standing ~/mvo-epistemic on aletheia-core (currentRegistry_accurate on propext alone in both; splice count 644 verified inside the def before building).
- phextura shadow: transaction 33 inserts / 15 replaces / 0 removes; 677/677 comparable scrolls identical to direct conversion; validator GREEN (char accounting 64,320 = 12 × 5,360 rewrites; checksum ok); NI from the transaction log equals the canonical NI (0.0788). AFTER score committed in thirst-quest (eb4610c). Mastery entry #10 published to wbic16/agi@exo at commit 54e40ed2 (remote bytes verified, sha256 3d1f552d0685ad0abe63dbdb2fd7b1b850d57634bedd1c22a091d5abc7da7929).

Results:
- research.phext: 644 scrolls, 222 concepts, narrative v24, Oracle ~80% (70–90); Singular audit residual 0; research.index.json regenerated (644 entries).
- research-tracker git: builder iterations through 40be6a8; epistemic/shadow commit ed33165.
# Find good upcoming online AI-focused hackathons we could compete in

Coordinate: 23.6.8/9.9.14/11.6.10
