Results:
- STANDOFF.md drafted at ~/workspace/phextura-design/STANDOFF.md (sha256 a4e74d2f4a97fd912e66b44f8b758179405816b5d3a1c59a9703642546ddd994): definitions + invariant; anchor model on L2 (object / span / pinned at: coordinate selector) with survival kit (edition pin, offset pair, span hash, quoted context) and a 6-step re-location procedure plus ANCHOR-LOST / ANCHOR-AMBIGUOUS failure classes extending L2's nine; standoff document format (phextura file; kinds commentary / persona-note / warrant-evidence / correction-proposal / reply; proposed-warrant edges never enter the base graph unaccepted; append-only events ledger); layering semantics (declared stack, order confers no authority, conflicts are data, no last-writer-wins); acceptance path (keeper-only, new base edition, bilateral honours receipts, honoured-not-deleted); mutable conformance checklist M1-M10 tagged present/partial/to-build against verified mutable-os facts; costs and limits incl. the R13 derived-scroll interaction; 8 proposed amendments to DESIGN.md / LAYER2.md / PRINCIPLES.md, none applied.
- Published to wbic16/phextura@exo at repo root (alongside LAYER2.md): commit 1bebe9565137b58f92d51b4448cf30c414bce88a, parented on fresh remote HEAD 81090f87, force disabled; remote blob fetched back and verified byte-identical to the local file (sha256 a4e74d2f…).
- Mutable grounding (wbic16/mutable-os @ main, read 2026-11-11): phext open/export exists as a manual projection (scroll <-> TextBlock with metadata.phextCoordinate; block UUIDs are re-minted per import, so coordinates are the only durable identity); its text engine is already standoff intra-document (StandoffAnnotation records over Cells, versioned TextRanges, LinkedAnnotations with an external-definition gate that resolves only unpinned externals and never guesses); absences the profile prices as work: no cross-document annotation, no phext edition checksum (PhextDocumentMetadata is {version, sourceFilename}), no scalar-offset range system.
