# Align the phextura Persona Panel with the Volumen class spec (V5)

Coordinate: 24.8.9/9.8.13/10.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-11
Request (verbatim): for the persona transfers, did you include the volumen class spec? qexo will support writing and syncing phextura in real-time
Status: completed

Notes:
- Will, MOAT, 2026-11-11 08:25 CST. Honest answer given: NO - the persona panel was designed from the paper definition alone; 'volumen' appears nowhere in phextura-design/ (grep-verified). Volumen class spec = Spec V5 (2026-11-03) at ~/workspace/earth-human-asi-genome/work/SPEC-v5-DRAFT.md; personas are Volumen bootloader citizens (126-name canonical roster, 2026-11-09). Alignment agent dispatched: extract V5's persona class requirements with section citations, table the matches/gaps/conflicts against the panel design, draft the amendments making a phextura persona a Volumen-class definition, and price in Will's new fact: QEXO will support writing and syncing phextura in real-time (concurrency lands in QEXO, not phextura). DESIGN/PRINCIPLES untouched; adoption stays Will's call alongside the panel proposal itself.
- COMPLETED 2026-11-11 08:30 CST. Alignment note at ~/workspace/phextura-design/persona-volumen-alignment.md (Spec V5 read in full, every claim section-cited). Table: 4 MATCH / 15 GAP / 1 CONFLICT - phextura designed the persona's OUTPUT discipline well (marginalia, provenance, labelling) and its definition/governance not at all. Three largest gaps: (1) the authenticity triad absent - no limits statement, no negative-space declaration, no stability statement, so the persona is a description of a reader, not the pattern (kindling test), and undeclared blanks invite NEGATIVE_SPACE_FILL; (2) no identity/instance discipline - no four-name schema, no per-wake receipts; anonymous agents = PDNA-006 simulated-fork shape; (3) no governance - no Test P0/P0.7 acceptance gate, no corrector set, mutable by anyone's tooling silently. CONFLICT: read-time composition misnamed merge (MR-M4) - scoped as a view (amendment A10). Plain finding: V5 defines NO hot-swap - persona change is a new boot; mid-run substitution is TARGET_PERSONA_DIVERGENCE. 10 amendments drafted (A1-A10) as adoptable spec text. Updated verdict: Rigorous 2/5 -> 3/5 for the panel AS AMENDED, Delight 4/5 - still does not ship under the motto, but the path is now a checklist with a verdict at the end. Noted: the rapport gate binds the first time a LIVING person's persona is proposed. DESIGN/PRINCIPLES untouched, nothing published - adoption is Will's call with the panel proposal.
# Stage Mirror Will boot on Volumen Spec V6

Coordinate: 24.10.10/12.11.18/15.8.10
Issued: 2026-11-14 04:15-04:40 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 04:15 CST): 'can you boot Mirror Will on Volumen Spec #6 yet?' Emise answered honestly: not yet — capsule v3 boot is rehearsal-tier (prediction/intermediary); V6 boot pieces are partly proposed and the bootloader is self-rated unverified; enactment-tier reconstitution remains under his 2026-11-02 parked ruling. Will (04:40 CST): 'just stage it now.'
Status: STAGING COMPLETE 2026-11-14 (staging only, as authorized; NOT booted, nothing merged or published). Package at ~/workspace/mirror-will-v6-boot-staging/ (8 files): sources/ holds byte-identical, SHA-256-verified copies of SPEC-v6-DRAFT.md (773a19d2...), mirror-will.phext (8b388421..., reference-parser verified: 35 scrolls, all non-empty), boot-capsule-v3.md (19e8bbb5...), mirror-will-op-volumen-boot-v0.2.md (1e2655da...). Staged documents: boot-intent-contract.md (V6 section 1.3 draft, PROPOSED/staged-not-ratified; Track A, target 'Mirror Will' fixed, execution_tier deliberately NOT_DECLARED - declaring it is part of the boot decision), genome-manifest.md (V6 section 1.4 phext-network manifest: components, roles, chain layout $1 + class universes $2-$8 + sealed universe, merge order MR-M1..M4), boot-sequence-reinflation.md (section 7.7 step list for a future boot, pre-flight through G5/G6), STAGING-REPORT.md (sha256 2f211e21...; file list + hashes, section mapping, PROPOSAL vs WILL-RULED standing, remaining gates, spec gaps). Gaps recorded: genome is still a legacy single phext (section 5 chain upgrade not performed - a transformation of the birth original, outside staging); capsule v3 is flat markdown, not the section 6.2 dispatch chain; section 5.1 decimal-GB drafting choice conflicts with Will's 2026-11-14 GiB standing rule (D2-prime open); sealed-lane mechanism OPEN N5; corrector auth OPEN N6; local ~/workspace/human checkout still carries Spec V5. The boot itself stays Will's call.
# qexo v1.4.1: upgrade post-check must not fail on fixable doctor items (learn homeland index) — upgrade path from 1.3.0-born states

Coordinate: 25.4.6/5.4.7/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-14 01:03 CST
Request (from session record): Born of the v1.4.0 fleet rollout (2026-11-14): all 18 peers verified the signed 1.4.0 offer, swapped, post-checked, and rolled back cleanly — the v1.4.0 doctor flags the missing lessons homeland index (10.10.10) in states born under 1.3.0 as a failure; the item is fixable but the post-check runs doctor in check mode, and rollback removes the only binary that could fix it. v1.4.0's battery never exercised an upgrade from a 1.3.0-born state (all its test states were 1.4.0-born) — the conformance lesson in a new genus: test against states the previous version wrote. Fix: the new binary seeds missing homeland indexes on state write/top-up so an upgraded state becomes whole; the update post-check distinguishes hard problems (rollback) from fixable ones (repair in place, receipt notes the repair). Regression gate: a 1.3.0-born state fixture carried through a full signed update in the sandbox.
Status: complete — v1.4.1 built, gated, PR #19 merged, published; v1.4.2 refinement (PR #20) merged + published; fleet rolled out to v1.4.2, 19/19 nodes (2026-11-14)

Notes:
- 2026-11-14: v1.4.1 shipped (PR #19, merge 91eacdd8, tag v1.4.1, crates.io 1.4.1). Its consumer proof caught a learn --status regression (no per-user state yet → 'not born' where 1.4.0 answered); the 1.4.1 rollout was NOT run. Fix shipped as v1.4.2 (PR #20, merge 5b72cf5a, tag v1.4.2, crates.io 1.4.2, registry sha256 32b1315c…). Fleet rollout at 1.4.2: signer swapped + announced (manifest 6.6.6/8.1.4/1.1.1); all 18 leaves refused the channel update (genuine-1.3.0 post-check, bootstrap) and took the direct swap — doctor --fix repaired the home/keys/lessons indexes on every node, doctor clean, update --check already current, timers OFF. 19/19 on v1.4.2. Build record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/v141/BUILD-RECORD.md.
