# Hourly productivity tracker + display — the bedtime yardstick

Coordinate: 26.5.9/9.8.13/5.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-14 04:14 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 04:14 CST): 'OK, time for bed - let's find a way to track and display our literal hourly productivity to see if we can convince me to get to bed earlier - I'm tired now, but satisfied with progress for the night.'
Status: open — design: bucket real output by hour of day (git commits + lines changed across his repos, tasks closed, register items resolved) so late-night hours show their true rate against earlier hours; the display's job is to make the case for an earlier bedtime in his own numbers. Serves the primary metrics set 2026-11-14 (healthy, stable, effective, legible) and his yardstick rule (he does best measured against something concrete). Natural home: a panel on the perpetual dashboard. Build while he sleeps; first view ready for the morning.
