# Newt — mesh-networked musical instruments, Android prototype

Coordinate: 26.7.9/8.7.12/8.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-13 22:36 CST
Request (verbatim): Newt

musical instruments that automatically mesh network via Wi-Fi when near each other. prototype on Android immediately. rules below: 

A local group of newts is called an Armada. 
The global group is called a Maelstrom. 

gameplay: 
players can start a song whenever
tapping produces entropy in 9D space using holographic time
the notes produced are rendered according to rules that evolve as we coordinate organically
the spine of famous songs is included as gravity
after a song is recorded, it becomes part of the global lexicon, obviously encoded in music.phext

ask me any clarifying questions needed
Status: v0.3.0 delivered 2026-11-14 — N3 revision built and delivered in the Newt side chat; awaiting Will's on-device verdict

Notes:
- Will's spec answers (2026-11-13 22:42 CST): (1) pairing code on the same WiFi network; (2) test devices: Pixel 10 XL and Samsung Galaxy S25; (3) tap position and velocity matter; player picks instrument type — string, flute, or synth; (4) both — the song follows a path, players provide entropy and motion; (5) players can choose how wild the song is; (6) Newts are named by the player; songs follow lyrics — public domain or uploaded lyrics; (7) the proposed v0 done-bar is the MVP: 2+ phones auto-discover as an Armada (with pairing code), a tap on one plays on all in sync, Stop records the song, exports music.phext that reopens and replays.
- MVP built 2026-11-13 evening: Android app (single-activity Java, no third-party deps) compiled on aletheia-core with a fresh JDK 21 + Android SDK 34 toolchain under ~/newt-build (Gradle 8.7, AGP 8.5.2). APK: ~/workspace/newt-proto/out/Newt-0.1.0.apk, 32,537 B, SHA-256 01f5dcadc044dc0620d2525a2ab84311986f70dc69cc845459f7f9200a1fddb2, debug-signed, apksigner verified. music.phext format verified with parse_phext.py: song headers at chapter starts (1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.1, .../2.1.1), one scroll per note event. Source + README + build scripts: ~/workspace/newt-proto/. NOT yet run on a physical phone — Will's Pixel 10 XL / Galaxy S25 two-phone test is the next leg.
- On-device test (Will, 2026-11-13 23:28-23:36 CST): v0.1.0 sideloaded and worked on the first try; solo mode confirmed as the way he trials the APK. N2 notes (Will, 2026-11-13 23:43 CST): audio clips are harsh; auto-chord from the tap region; smooth audio driven by velocity instead of position; soothing out of the box ('vibes of solitudes'); 300 Hz-3 kHz core band, higher notes quieter; follow the musical universe of Bach; polished UI / Phext Blue branding; play the Phext P3 logo audio on startup.
