- Start from the two images Will uploaded 2026-11-09: the flame-and-scroll-wall banner (the site's own banner art, made 2026-11-08) and a backlit-keyboard mood shot. Scope refined by Will: favicon.ico specifically. Current site favicon is a gem/diamond SVG with color bands.
- Will chose concept A (flame alone) over B (flame + lattice) and C (banner crop) on 2026-11-09 19:34 CST.
- PR #32 (edit-art wiring) found MERGED 2026-11-09 04:23 UTC, so the favicon went on a fresh branch off exo HEAD 9458cb10: emise/favicon-flame-banner-optimize, commit 405db007, PR #40. Replaced web/favicon.ico (1,746->4,313 B), web/favicon.svg (575->858 B), web/apple-touch-icon.png (2,078->13,356 B); added web/favicon-512.png (61,682 B) beside og.png (not referenced by any route yet). All blobs verified vs remote tree; cargo test --release on aletheia-core: exit 0, 235 passed / 0 failed.

Results:
- Production set built in ~/workspace/favicon-work/: favicon.ico (16/32/48 in one 4,313 B file; 16px render uses an enlarged flame for legibility), favicon.svg (858 B hand-authored vector twin, render-verified), apple-touch-icon.png (180x180), favicon-512.png.
- PR #40 open against exo: https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/40 — merging is Will's.
- AUDIT 2026-11-12 (tasks.phext verification pass): STALE-DONE — phext-lattice PR #40 MERGED (audit merge-check, 2026-11-12); favicon live-verified on edit.phext.io (register #51 resolution). Prior status read: "PR #40 open — flame favicon wired, merge is Will's"
