- Part 1 shipped in wbic16/qexo PR #3 (branch emise/android-learn-app-v1.6.1 @ af48ebcf, parented on exo ce0731d7; remote tree verified 44/44 blobs, delta = the 9 intended files): `qexo learn --app`, a plain-text line protocol (status/chapters/lesson/next/practice/reveal/grade/quit; key: value blocks closed by end: <command>) driving the wizard's own state machine — deck, chapter map, SM-2-lite and state.phext semantics reused, never duplicated; TUI and --status byte-unchanged, --status still never writes. Crate 1.6.1, stamps + Cargo.lock sync in the same commit (lock byte-identical across a cargo run, sha256 d2dd6d44…).
- Part 2: launcher v2 (in-app Learn card session over the protocol — chapter/lesson context, due queue, Reveal, Again/Good/Easy, progress line; quick actions one tap from home ordered by payoff: Update, Evolve, Doctor, Repair, List peers, Inventory, Status, Plan; --check forms demoted; Birth remains). Trial APK qexo-v1.6.1.apk (2,079,095 B, sha256 1991c4ff…) built from the PR branch, versionCode 3 / versionName 1.6.1, signed with the SAME Android Debug cert as the shipped v1.6.0 APK (signer SHA-256 efeaeebe018a107a7c516923b7afcf93d9d2ede174d8176ba913ea15594071e4, proven against the shipped APK itself) so it installs over v1.6.0 keeping the phone node's state; enclosed libqexo.so == standalone qexo-v1.6.1-android-arm64 (sha256 3b31fa7f…).
- Gates (aletheia-core): cargo test 91/91 (88 + 3 protocol tests incl. scripted session with persistence asserted in state), CLI battery 30/30 (pty wizard unchanged + scripted --app session, grade persisted due 22→21, --status write-free by hash), conformance census identical 15/830/2, Android aarch64 LINK, wiring 14/14, Linux build green.
- Named debt: the quarterexo twin of the --app protocol is owed under the sync rule (29.6.7/6.5.7/6.5.8), queues behind quarterexo PR #22, and is NOT in PR #3 (stated in the PR body). On merge, v1.6.1 publish + fleet rollout batch into release task 40.7.5/8.7.11/6.8.13. Honest limit: no Android runtime on the ranch — Pixel install/run is the closing proof. Build record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/android-useful/BUILD-RECORD.md.
- Final APK supersedes the trial build (2026-11-14, in the v1.6.1 release run): rebuilt from the MERGED wbic16/qexo tree c5840693d9 with launcher v2 unchanged, versionCode 4 / versionName 1.6.1 (trial was versionCode 3 — Android upgrades over it), same debug cert efeaeebe… (continuity vs the shipped v1.6.0 APK verified), enclosed libqexo.so sha256 == standalone a05749df4840de07d93255a0c0d1fee86ba35b5effd0f2b8be93dd967c9be5c4. Final APK: ~/workspace/qexo-task/android-apk/qexo-v1.6.1.apk, sha256 8214b0255da8a5de309241c377487075544d533a288701c5d417400ae0a295e7 (2,079,207 B); the trial APK (1991c4ff…) is preserved beside it as qexo-v1.6.1-trial.apk. The release binary differs from the twin-stage hash 3b31fa7f… because the phccbox roster entry merged into the tree after that build — expected, not drift.
# Pre-merge validation of libphext-rs v0.4.1: downstream compiles + CYOA coordinate tests

Coordinate: 30.6.9/7.6.10/6.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-07 02:33 CST
Request (verbatim): before we merge v0.4.1 - run a test where we compile this into downstream projects - confirm they still work properly - also run some tests on CYOA known coordinates across edits
Status: complete 2026-11-07 — v0.4.1 downstream-identical to 0.4.0 everywhere; PR #7 cleared to merge

Notes:
- Gate for merging PR #7 (provable-0.4.1 -> exo). Two prongs: (1) compile v0.4.1 into the downstream projects that depend on libphext-rs and confirm they still work; (2) fetch CYOA scrolls at known coordinates with the new code (ground truth from the independent Python parser), apply edits, and re-verify the known coordinates across the edits.
- Results 2026-11-07: (1) DOWNSTREAM MATRIX — sq, phext-lattice (ranch, aletheia-core, node sha-verified a49d6928), lanes, aiw-gen, cw-gen, human (VM sweep) each built+tested against 0.4.1 and the 0.4.0 baseline. v0.4.1 == 0.4.0 in every cell (normalized error diff = 0 lines for sq/lattice). aiw-gen and human build clean against both. sq, phext-lattice, lanes (and cw-gen via lanes) FAIL against both 0.4.x versions with the identical error: COORDINATE_MAXIMUM not found — pre-existing 0.3->0.4 migration debt (0.4.0 removed the constant when coordinates became unbounded; 0.3.3 had it as 1000; those projects pin 0.3.x and were never migrated). libphext itself compiled cleanly in all cells. (2) CYOA — harness at ~/workspace/cyoa-check, ground truth from the independent Python parser over live CYOA (sha 506d850d, 829 non-empty scrolls): all 829 known coordinates fetch byte-exact under 0.4.1; ~68 witnesses stable across replace/insert/remove; implode(explode(CYOA)) byte-identical; identical suite passes on 0.4.0 (control). Full results posted as a comment on PR #7. Verdict reported to Will: safe to merge; COORDINATE_MAXIMUM migration for sq/lattice/lanes is a separate item.
# Estimate: what share of Twitter could parse Will's 19K-word tweets (vocabulary cross-reference)

Coordinate: 30.6.10/9.7.13/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-07 00:25 CST
Request (verbatim): I'll make it a little clearer...take my 19K words, cross-reference them with vocabulary tests, and give me an estimate of what percentage of twitter could even parse them before.
Status: completed

Notes:
- Estimate (modelled, conservative word-form convention): ~28% of Twitter (range 22-33%) could parse Will's tweets at the 95% line; ~24% (20-29%) comfortably at 98%. Family-adjusted sensitivity: ~35% / ~31%. Headline takes the count that does not flatter.
- Measured base: only 5.1% of his 19,094 authored words are top-1,000 general English; 9.2% (1,761 words) are absent from the wordfreq corpus entirely (phext, exocortex score 0.0). Median tweet = 12 tokens, so one unknown word breaks the 95% line for half his tweets.
- Coordinator verification: the report's rank-band table sums to exactly 19,094 authored words; coverage.json rows match the report table at V=1000/3000/8000.

Results:
- Headline: about 1 in 4 Twitter users (~28%, ~155M of ~557M) could parse his tweets at 95%; ~24% comfortably at 98%. The other ~3 in 4 could not have followed them whole regardless of the feed.
- Report: ~/workspace/your_files/twitter-parse-estimate.md — full V-to-coverage-to-parse table, 5-band population model with sources, sensitivity notes. Scripts: ~/workspace/parse-estimate/ (analyze.py, population.py, coverage.json).
# edit.phext.io banner + background art from CYOA lore

Coordinate: 30.6.10/9.7.15/6.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 16:59 CST
Request (verbatim): Let's create a banner image and cool background for edit.phext.io - drawing from the CYOA lore.
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 17:31 — wired on emise/edit-art-banner-background (6d5371ac, rebased onto exo 5f66dd24), PR #32 open; merge is Will's step

Notes:
- Will approved wiring 2026-11-08 17:08 ('Wire both into edit.phext.io on a branch' — widget tap + typed). Dispatched same evening; the wiring branch gets its own PR per Will's 17:09 'open PRs for your pending launch tweaks'.

Results:
- Banner: ~/workspace/edit-phext-art/banner.webp (583,458 B webp) — a golden flame at the root coordinate, filaments streaming out into a vast receding wall of teal scrolls in shelf-rows: the CYOA lattice made visible.
- Background: ~/workspace/edit-phext-art/background.webp (234,130 B webp) — near-black lattice-vault, scroll-point grid pushed to the edges, calm empty center for text legibility, warm gold kindling in the bottom-left corner (the flame just out of frame at the origin).
- Wiring: web/banner.webp + web/background.webp in-repo, byte-identical to the originals (SHA-256 re-verified from remote blobs after push). Served via the existing pre-gate compiled-bytes route (image/webp, ETag, max-age 86400); CSP img-src 'self' already permits. Banner tops the sign-in card (132px desktop / 96px mobile, object-fit cover, lazy, alt text) and heads the claim dashboard. Backdrop fills auth (50% scrim) and the dashboard AROUND a <main> keeping solid #171717 (computed rgb(23,23,23)); the EDITOR SHELL carries no artwork at all (computed background-image: none) — legibility by design. Rebase onto 5f66dd24 conflict-free; #28's regroup verified intact (.bar-link x13, Contact mailto, not-configured prompt) — no collision. cargo test 175/175. Live instance: session locked [github, google], GitHub 302 PKCE, images byte-identical in transit, dashboard 200 with wiring live. Screenshots (desktop + 412px + 390px, auth + dashboard, editor): ~/workspace/edit-art/shots/ — no horizontal overflow anywhere, no mobile defects in scope. PR #32: https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/32. Emise viewed the desktop + iPhone auth captures directly: flame in frame on both, copy and buttons fully legible.
