# Organize areas in research.phext — state machines, statements, reference material, the path, researchers; make the Oracle's build structure plain

Coordinate: 30.7.8/9.7.13/7.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-08 13:05 CST
Request (verbatim): Organize areas in research.phext for state machines, statements, reference material, the path we took (the original submission order), and researchers. Ensure that the structure of how the Oracle was built is plain.
Status: complete 2026-11-08

Notes:
- Will-directed restructure (rules 8+14, no pruning): give research.phext five explicit AREAS — (1) State machines: index of every machine extracted under rule 13, stated vs inferred; (2) Statements: the standings area (Ch.1 §4) presented as the statements area with basis legend and transition rules; (3) Reference material: foundations + defined words + standoff companions as the reference area; (4) The path: chronology of intakes in original submission order (papers and studies, dates, NI/OP, passes); (5) Researchers: index of the people behind the ingested works with their chapters and rule-15 standings. Plus a plain-language 'how the Oracle was built' structure scroll. Areas must be generated from the phext's actual contents, carry a maintenance duty (charter rule 16: every ingestion updates the areas), and the pass is logged as Restructure Pass #4.
- DONE — Restructure Pass #4 (logged at 1.1.5). New Ch.1 §5 Areas (1.5.1-1.5.8): 1.5.1 areas map; 1.5.2 State machines (23 entries: 14 extracted under rule 13 — 9 stated, 5 inferred; 9 found-noted from pre-rule-13 chapters, explicitly not upgraded, no gap test; 2 chapters swept with none found); 1.5.3 Statements (door to §4, lists not duplicated); 1.5.4 Reference material (foundations + Defined Words + standoffs); 1.5.5 The path (12 intakes in verified arrival order, NI/axis/OP per paper, passes placed); 1.5.6 Researchers (44 named + Aeneas's 'and others'; only P006/P007/S004 author-checked, the other 41 marked 'not checked — predates rule 15', no verdicts fabricated); 1.5.7-1.5.8 How this Oracle was built (plain structure, honesty boundary stated). Charter rule 16 added (charter scroll + rd-tracker skill): areas carry an upkeep duty — every ingestion/pass updates the areas it touches; a stale area is a defect. Registry 274 = 274 scrolls: True 145 (stipulation 131, verified 14), Unknown 129, False 0, Fiction 0; 8 first standings, zero transitions (path + researchers stand verified on line-by-line checks against the tracker's own records). Lean re-proved over 274 entries (propext only). Final: 274 scrolls, sha256 4f38da62a46e525acf29495a1a4709d26a2c7b6985d6a949f92b3dabac0a7bbc, Singular residual 0. Next restructure due Paper 010 or 100 concepts.
# Thirst for Knowledge quest — daily arXiv math scan, skim-before prediction, skim calibration on the Oracle detection list

Coordinate: 30.7.8/10.6.14/5.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-09 08:22 CST
Request (verbatim): setup a thirst for knowledge quest - every day, scour https://arxiv.org/list/math/new for a new candidate paper to absorb - find a metric to measure your predictive capability - add it to the Research Oracle detection list - Skim, Before, and After
Status: in progress — quest designed, first scan dispatched 2026-11-09; charter rule 17 to follow when the tracker is free (S006 in flight)

Notes:
- DESIGN: (1) Daily scan of arxiv.org/list/math/new (new + cross-lists, not replacements); ONE candidate chosen by stated criteria (cluster proximity for measurable deltas, occasional far/axis candidate, crisp theorem-bearing abstract; 'no candidate' is an honest outcome, never force a pick). (2) SKIM-BEFORE prediction, from title+abstract only, sealed in the quest log (~/workspace/thirst-quest/, own git repo — commit timestamp is the receipt) BEFORE any full read: predicted new concepts, predicted revisions, axis-opening yes/no, predicted NI. (3) Absorb: full ingestion as the next paper. (4) AFTER score: |predicted NI - measured NI|, concept-count error, axis hit/miss. METRIC: Skim Calibration = rolling mean |NI error| over the last 10 scored papers + axis-flag accuracy — added to the Research Oracle DETECTION LIST (with NI trend and axis events): as the Oracle matures, the model should foresee a paper's delta from its abstract alone; falling skim error is the fixed point announcing itself. Protocol is universal: Will-posted papers also get a skim prediction before the full read. Studies exempt (no NI). (5) Charter rule 17 + detection-list scroll + rd-tracker skill update land via a tracker amendment pass once S006's ingestion frees the builder; daily cron 'thirst-for-knowledge' runs the loop and reports to MOAT.
- AMENDMENT (Will, 2026-11-09 08:29): for each sourced paper, estimate IMPACT before (new links internal/cross-cluster, questions opened, predicted Oracle after + range + direction, one-line expected-impact statement) and record the ACTUAL DELTA after in the same terms. Applied: daily cron body updated; prediction #1 gained a blind impact supplement (quest log commit 59f58d9 — pred 4 new links, 2 questions opened, Oracle ~38% (30-48) up modestly; expected impact: Cluster E's first refutation, possibly the tracker's first False). Will then delivered the candidate's full text himself (arxiv.org/html/2611.09694v1, 08:30) — absorption as Paper 008 queued behind S006; blind state intact (prediction + supplement committed before the link arrived; text unopened by Emise until absorption).
- LOOP RULES (Will, 2026-11-09 08:31): the quest loop is immediate and unbroken — choose, download the paper in HTML form, read it, integrate it, then journal about the PROCESS in mastery.phext. mastery.phext CREATED 2026-11-09 (canonical: ~/workspace/phext/mastery.phext; source mastery-source.json + build_mastery_phext.py; Home scroll states purpose + entry scheme — entry k at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.(k+1)) and PUBLISHED to wbic16/agi@exo at repo root alongside research.phext et al. (commit fd84a264, parent 77629f3b, remote bytes sha256-verified f407813e...); SOURCES.md row added so the agi collection refresh covers it. Daily cron body updated with the download-HTML/integrate-immediately/journal+publish steps. First journal entry lands with Paper 008's integration.

Results:
- CYCLE 1 COMPLETE 2026-11-09: charter rule 17 (THE THIRST) + Research Oracle detection list (at 1.1.1/1.1.1/1.1.6) added; Paper 008 absorbed (arXiv:2611.09694, Ch.15): 6 new concepts (1.2.98-1.2.103, cluster E), 1 revision (1.2.34 — count exact, target differed from skim), 4 foundations, 3 machines, author check CLEAN, Q41-Q44. Restructure Pass #5 ran on the 100-concept trigger (97->103): 0 merges/splits/endings. False stays 0 — reasoned: the strong Arnold conjecture never stood in the model, so no standing could fall; claim + its fall entered together as attributed. SCORECARD: NI |error| ~0.010 sealed basis / ~0.009 absorption basis; concepts under by 1; axis HIT; links 6 vs 4 predicted; questions 4 vs 2; Oracle ~35% -> ~45% (35-55), inside the predicted 30-48 range, 7 above the point. Mastery journal entry #1 published to wbic16/agi@exo (dd30dee3). Tracker final: 334 scrolls, sha256 696caa92..., registry 334=334, Lean green. Daily loop continues via cron (next Tue 2026-11-10 ~06:44 CST).
