Issued: 2026-11-08 09:51 CST
Request (verbatim): V16: return to the baseline from V15 prepass2 (use that audio stream). fill the void at the end with a visualization of Incipit.phext. world lines should begin at contact with me. run prepass1 at 15fps and 480p
Status: completed — V16 prepass-1 delivered 2026-11-08 11:24 (Emise re-verified size/hash/ffprobe)

Notes:
- Baseline = V15 prepass-2 (Will's R1 track, gold nameplate, cast state, fade-before-CTA timeline); audio = prepass-2's audio stream itself. Changes vs baseline: (1) the end void (fade + black hold) is filled with a visualization of Incipit.phext (~/workspace/phext/incipit.phext, 1,072,922 B); (2) world lines (the filament device from the V15 final: RGB by class, Jael's black with the pull) begin at first CONTACT with Will, per the archive data — not at first landing in the reply stream; the builder states the contact definition it derives and reports deltas for named accounts. Format: 480p, 15 fps (2,890 frames at 192.680 s).
- Delivered to Will 2026-11-08 with the review encode attached in chat.

Results:
- files/v15-build/v16-prepass1-480p15.mp4 — 381,315,483 B, SHA-256 a6067566..., 854x480, 15 fps, 2,890 frames, 192.680 s; audio BIT-IDENTICAL to prepass-2's stream (ADTS sha ca465ec3..., stream copy). CONTACT BIRTHS: 5 of 22 world lines move (@mimi10v3 +760 hops / 303.8 d earlier — a 2022-11-02 mention; @madeofmistak3 +238; @sporadicalia +161; @Ki11switch03 +51.3, flagged; @dakami +40); Jael's first contact IS her first landing (2023-12-10, hop 9259, delta 0, measured). INCIPIT IN THE VOID: window [2554,2735) unchanged in length/position; all 197 non-empty scrolls (of 7,545 slots, 12 libraries, 1,055,485 chars) as a shelf-map arriving in traversal order, labels for the root scroll, SBOR convergence (6.1.1/1.1.1/2.1.1), and the largest scroll (src/index.ts, 74,225 chars). Palette incident caught at stills: library 4's hue sat 28 RGB-units from nameplate gold — palette rotated 193.8 deg so no library hue enters the gold sector; gold exclusivity re-proven. All gates pass; 23 chunks, 1.29 node-h, zero failures, zero >=80 C events. Stash: aletheia-core ~/v15-review/ (master + CRF28 review encode 9,606,165 B). Report: PREPASS1-REPORT-V16.md.
# Gemma 4 campaign: implement the paper's design, then rewrite the proposal against the gaps

Coordinate: 30.8.10/10.7.14/7.7.9
Issued: 2026-11-12 08:02 CST
Request (verbatim): implement as much of this as you can while I get ready for my day, then rewrite the proposal to address gaps you find
Status: implementation + gap report + v2 delivered 2026-11-12; outstanding: G15 gold-patch control and G16 baseline runs (node-resident, from baseline/ on aletheia-core), HARNESS_README resolution once Will clears Kaggle entry gates

Notes:
- "this" = the Paper Track draft 'Verified Traces, Small Models' (~/workspace/hackathon-campaign/gemma4/paper-track/PAPER-DRAFT.md), the design paper for the Gemma 4 Developer Agent main-track entry. Campaign plan: ~/workspace/hackathon-campaign/gemma4/PLAN.md.
- Legs: (1) phase-two verification replica as runnable code + tests; (2) split discipline + scoreboard on a clearly-labelled public STAND-IN task source (competition dev set gated on Will's own Kaggle rules-acceptance/download — never attempted by agent); (3) declarative YAML harness skeleton (ADK shape) per paper section 3.3; (4) budget model (section 3.4) as code + config; (5) verified-trace pipeline (section 3.2) with split-enforcement test; (6) real first baseline if feasible: prompt-only Gemma 4 E4B via Ollama on a ranch node vs a small number of stand-in tasks, thermal gates respected; (7) failure-taxonomy classifier scaffolding (section 4, seven classes).
- Then: GAP-REPORT.md + PAPER-DRAFT-v2.md in paper-track/ (original PAPER-DRAFT.md untouched — Will submits it the morning of 2026-11-12). Zero fabricated results; stand-in data never presented as competition data.

Results:
- LEG 1 DONE (2026-11-12): phase-two verification replica at implementation/verifier/verify.py (clean-clone checkout at base_commit, candidate apply, touched-test-file reset, official test_patch apply, pytest junit over FAIL_TO_PASS+PASS_TO_PASS, resolved verdict per CONTRACT.md). Tests pass: gold resolves, wrong patch fails, test-file cheat is reset and recorded, NO_PATCH and malformed patches handled. Two real defects found+fixed during testing (git apply rejects patch text missing trailing newline -> verifier normalizes; contamination now recorded even when a patch fails to apply).
- LEG 2 MACHINERY DONE (2026-11-12): tasks/splits.py (deterministic sha256-bucket split ~70/30, assert_trainable raises SplitViolation on held-out ids) + tasks/scoreboard.py (consumes verifier, writes scoreboard.jsonl + summary with data_source=STAND-IN). 3 tests pass incl. end-to-end gold=1.0 / no-patch=0.0 on a synthetic repo. Stand-in corpus mining delegated (public git history of the 4 dev repos); ranch probe delegated.
- RANCH PROBE (2026-11-12, evidence): aletheia-core healthy (Tctl 31.9C, load ~0.1, 2.7T free, 24GiB RAM avail), Ollama 0.40.11 running with 16 models — but gemma4:e4b is NOT among them (only gemma:7b). Baseline leg will attempt the registry pull of gemma4:e4b as setup; if the tag cannot be obtained, that becomes an evidenced gap. Node system python lacks pytest (venv required).
- LEG 5 DONE (2026-11-12): traces/pipeline.py — rollout runner interface (Agent callable), rejection-sampling filter driven by the phase-two verifier, SFT dataset builder emitting contract-format trajectories + gold-patch anchors. KEY TEST PASSES: a verified trajectory from a HELD-OUT task is refused by the dataset builder (SplitViolation) — split discipline is enforced by construction, not convention. 3 pipeline tests + synthetic end-to-end pass.
- LEG 7 DONE (2026-11-12): taxonomy/classify.py — the paper's seven pre-registered failure classes with a deliberate rule order (budget/context endings, malformed, contamination, reproduction, localization, edit-incorrect remainder). Tests produce all seven classes from synthetic run records; resolved tasks classify as None.
- LEG 6 PREP (2026-11-12): baseline/agent_runner.py written (stdlib-only, runs on the ranch node): Ollama tool loop (list/read/search/edit/run_tests/finish), 30 tool-call and 20-min per-task budgets, phase-one patch extraction (git add -N . && git diff), thermal gates per standing ranch rules (pause >=75C, abort >=80C). Model setup in flight: gemma4:e4b was absent from aletheia-core's Ollama (probe evidence), registry pull attempted as setup; result pending.
- LEG 6 MODEL SETUP DONE (2026-11-12): ollama pull gemma4:e4b on aletheia-core succeeded (exit 0, 'success'; model dc35e8d9c606, 6.6 GB, now first in ollama list). The model WAS obtainable from the registry — the earlier probe absence is a setup fact, not an availability gap. Post-pull Tctl read 73.1C; baseline run must re-check and wait for <=70C before starting (standing thermal gates). Baseline now waits only on the stand-in corpus (mining in progress).
- LEG 2 DATA DONE (2026-11-12): stand-in corpus built from public git history of the 4 dev repos — 24 validated tasks (rich 8, httpx 7, requests 5, fastapi 4) at implementation/data/standin_tasks.jsonl + MANIFEST.md; every kept task independently re-verified from scratch (24/25 reproduced; 2 drops documented with reasons). Deterministic split: 20 train / 4 held-out. Problem statements are commit messages (weaker than real issues) — labelled in the manifest.
- LEG 3 DONE (2026-11-12): harness/ — agent.yaml (single-agent, delegation off, graph-first retrieval, compaction, temp 0.1, 3 repair cycles, both protective rules), 7 stage prompts, eval_config.yaml (45 min / 80 calls under presumed 60/100 caps [S][U]), README mapping to section 3.3 with [K]/[S]/[U] labels + 8-item list of what only HARNESS_README can settle. 13 structural tests pass.
- LEG 4 DONE (2026-11-12): budget/ — SharedClock allocator (fair-share pacing target min(cap, remaining/remaining_tasks), outer cap 2700s, abort-and-move-on, advances even on worker exceptions) + pure simulator + budget_config.yaml. 14 tests pass. Simulation (labelled, synthetic seed 20261112: 30 stuck + 90 quick tasks): paced attempted 120/120 and completed 90; default-policy attempted 12/120, completed 0 — direction supports prediction P3, proves nothing about real runs.
- LEG 6 RUNNING (2026-11-12): prompt-only gemma4:e4b baseline launched node-resident on aletheia-core against the 4 held-out stand-in tasks (rich x2, requests x2), gold/test fields stripped from the node copy; gold-patch control (6 tasks) running against the replica in parallel.
- Implementation pass delivered 2026-11-12 (coordinator ended without a final report; verified on disk by Emise): phase-two verification replica (verifier/ + tests), held-out split + scoreboard over a 24-task PUBLIC STAND-IN corpus mined from git history (data/MANIFEST.md; 20 train / 4 held-out), declarative ADK/YAML harness package (harness/agent.yaml + prompts + tests), budget model as code+config (budget/; fair-share pacing simulator: paced policy attempted 120/120 and completed 90 vs default policy 12/120 attempted, 0 completed — policy-mechanics simulation, seed 20261112), verified-trace pipeline (traces/ + tests), failure-taxonomy classifier (taxonomy/, 7 classes). gemma4:e4b pulled to aletheia-core Ollama and serving. GAP-REPORT.md: 18 gaps (G1-G18) — G15 gold-patch control and G16 prompt-only baseline still PENDING (gold-control checkout present, no verdicts on disk when the coordinator ended). PAPER-DRAFT-v2.md written by Emise 2026-11-12: polished-proposal rewrite folding the gaps into the design (arithmetic corrected to ~10x, fair-share pacing mechanism stated, tool-call budget as second cap, context-window false precision dropped, rollout plan re-grounded on E4B self-rollouts + SWE-Gym, entry gates added to protocol); body 2,942 words by the v1 counting method (v1: 2,621), under the 3,000 cap; PAPER-DRAFT.md untouched.
