# qexo v1.4.0: unprivileged reads, per-user install, nav-tree list, hostnames, qexo learn

Coordinate: 31.5.5/6.5.7/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-14 00:01 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 00:01 CST), after installing qexo 1.3.0 from crates.io himself: five tweaks — (1) `qexo list` should work without sudo rights; (2) support per-user install; (3) show nodes in a phext nav tree; (4) use hostnames instead of IPs; (5) add a `qexo learn` command that teaches the user qexo's capabilities via spaced repetition. (1)+(2) share a root: state at /var/lib/qexo is root-owned; generalize the Android home-fallback into a state-dir resolution (QEXO_STATE > system path when privileged/writable > per-user home path), reads never requiring sudo, the chosen path always printed. (4): peer records and displays carry hostnames (tailnet DNS names) — Will's standing rule: name every tailnet address, never report bare IPs. (5): phext-native deck + scheduling records in state.phext, SM-2-lite, interactive terminal sessions.
Status: complete — PR #18 merged by Will 2026-11-14; qexo 1.4.0 published to crates.io; fleet signed rollout attempted and refused fleet-wide at the post-check (v1.4.0 doctor vs 1.3.0-born states) — fix is a v1.4.1 decision for Will

Notes:
- 2026-11-14 00:04 CST addendum (Will): a sixth tweak — `qexo inventory`, an inventory of phext ecosystem products with install/launch instructions. Built in the same slice; the verb ships with alias `catalog`; --install is print-only (stated in the PR).
- 2026-11-14 00:09 CST addendum 2 (Will): the inventory's source is a census of EVERY wbic16 GitHub repo — bake only repos with published, useful artifacts. Census executed: 201 repos enumerated via the authenticated API (site-map cross-check clean — no repo invisible), releases checked for all 201, crates.io/PyPI/npm probed for every non-fork repo in its language with registry hits ownership-checked. Baked: 11 verified products. Excluded: 190 (71 forks; notable near-misses named with evidence). Full census: ~/workspace/qexo-task/v140/ROSTER-CENSUS.md.
- 2026-11-14: v1.4.0 built and gated on aletheia-core (own tree ~/qexo-v14; all state work sandboxed; the concurrent fleet rebirth untouched). Gates: cargo test 71/71 (52 baseline + 19 new), CLI battery 42/42, unprivileged proofs 3/3 in a mount namespace (unreadable-system reads land on per-user state; unprivileged per-user birth; root fallback note on a read-only system mount), interop vs the published crates.io qexo 1.3.0 (fresh cargo install as the foreign peer: registered with host derived live from its key, signed offer verified by update --check, gossip via evolve --check), conformance census identical to v1.3.0 (15/830/2 on the three foreign files), incident volume GREEN, wiring 14/14, windows-gnu LINK (qexo.exe 1,913,952 B, GetDiskFreeSpaceExW in, statvfs out), Android aarch64 LINK green.
- Shipped: PR #18 — https://github.com/wbic16/quarterexo/pull/18 (branch emise/qexo-v1.4.0 @ 2e8da189, parented on fresh exo 5574f214e7, force disabled, remote tree verified 39/39 blobs+modes). Build record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/v140/BUILD-RECORD.md. Learn deck: 22 cards in the new homeland 10.10.10/10.10.10/10.10.10 (cluster 2). State resolution order shipped exactly as stated in the PR body. Merges are Will's.

Results:
- MERGED: PR #18 (wbic16/quarterexo) merged by Will 2026-11-14; exo 3ebaba7b8e27bc4571e947ab34b158b41d74dea5 (ancestor-verified to carry branch head 2e8da189).
- PUBLISHED: qexo 1.4.0 live on crates.io 2026-11-14 (gates 71/71, package list, dry-run clean). Registry: max_version 1.4.0, license MIT, crate sha256 4c76777a02a98678ef4bcfd00c412faef78e2f890fc2f01c789791c6bc24727d, dep libphext ^0.6.0; sparse index 200. Consumer proof: fresh CARGO_HOME install runs; learn --status (22-card deck) and inventory (11 entries) answer.
- SIGNER: aletheia-core swapped directly to the 1.4.0 fleet build (linux sha256 064242e00f063c898ff1dd440bda699f1dabf36ec0c2493d82ae06ab2c4a4645; old binary kept as qexo.prev-1.3.0), serve restarted, 1.4.0 announced — manifest 6.6.6/8.1.3/1.1.1, signature 6.6.6/8.1.3/1.1.2. Windows exe staged at fleet-keys/qexo-v1.4.0.exe (sha256 77c03a6c0a370358322617edb9b49ffaacc83261ffea329742f9b845e2b5766b).
- ROLLOUT REFUSED (all 18 peers, identical, verbatim): 'qexo update: the new binary failed its post-check (the new binary's doctor reports problems against this node's state) — qexo.prev restored; the node still runs the previous binary'. Root cause reproduced in sandbox: v1.4.0 doctor's only complaint against a 1.3.0-born state is the missing learn index 10.10.10/10.10.10/10.10.10 (marked fixable via doctor --fix, which the post-check never runs). Every node rolled back cleanly to 1.3.0 with a rolled-back receipt; nothing hand-copied. Channel itself proven: yeet-max update --check sees the signed 1.4.0 offer.
- NEXT (Will's call): a v1.4.1 whose update post-check runs the repair pass for fixable doctor items (or seeds the learn index on state write) makes the fleet rollout a pure re-run of this pass. Records: qexo-task/v140/BUILD-RECORD.md publish+rollout sections; qexo-task/publish-v1.4.0/ scripts + node logs. Register #102 resolved.
