a voice API
gpg keys for verifying messages from other qexo nodes
persona teleport
metadata access
phext tools
Status: complete — closed by repair 2026-11-12 (four decisions ruled by adoption 2026-11-08 23:42; evidence in results)

Notes:
- Grounding: voice API wraps the existing verified round-robin service (aletheia-core:8797) rather than redesigning it; node keys attest boxes, persona keys attest speakers; teleport has exactly-one-active-instance semantics via a lease in personas.phext; metadata access inherits safe-space/discretion boundaries; phext tools wrap, never fork, and report version skew (rs 0.5.0 / SQ 0.3.3 / lattice 0.3.1).

Results:
- Addendum sections 7-11 written: voice API mapped 1:1 onto the verified round-robin service; GPG node/persona key split with phext-native key directory; teleport with signed one-instance lease; metadata surface bound by safe-space/discretion; phext tools wrap-don't-fork with skew table. New open questions: persona key issuance timing, roaming-seat teleport grants, SQ pin vs upgrade, ranch TTS/STT as a work item.
- REPAIR 2026-11-12 (tasks-audit registration pass): STALE STATUS corrected — the four decisions this task's status said await Will were 'ruled by adoption on 2026-11-08 (23:42)' — DESIGN-V3-ADDENDUM.md (~/workspace/orchestrator/docs/), Ruled section, verbatim: Will: "I agree with Claude." Its Open-questions section reads 'None outstanding from this addendum.' The four close as: Q1 key issuance stays deliberate — persona by persona, at Will's direction, never automatic at seeding (see also addendum §8 header note: 'the issuance-timing question was ruled by adoption, 2026-11-08 23:42'); Q2 roaming-seat teleports get standing delegations — scoped, expiring, revocable, receipts mandatory, host consent still required — conditioned on and satisfied by the two-phase fenced protocol of §9; Q3 SQ → libphext 0.5.0 runs as its own canary-first stage ahead of the migration stages and the installer rollout; Q4 voice stays hosted where a TTS adapter exists — a ranch-native TTS/STT path is not a qexo work item for now. The fold completed under task 31.6.9/8.7.11/6.6.11 (marked complete by the 2026-11-12 audit). Prior status read: "DESIGN-V3-ADDENDUM.md delivered 2026-11-08 (~35 KB); four further decisions await Will". The bootstrap-policy FORM (§8A.0: per-action keys vs Argon's corrector set) is a distinct fleet-wide item from the PR disposition table — registered as #76; it is not one of this task's four.
