# Fix edit.phext.io footer overflow on live v1.1.0

Coordinate: 31.7.7/7.6.11/6.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-09
Request (from session record): footer issues - it runs off the page - testing mcp now
Status: DONE — PR #49 merged by Will 2026-11-09 23:55:22 CST (merge 327fa929), in exo head c5da01ee, ships in v1.1.1. Root cause (measured): signed-in status-bar row ~2,201px min-content inside overflow-clip ancestors + dead height:auto in the 701-1100px band. Fix: 3 CSS lines (flex-wrap + min-height on base #status-bar rule, dead band height removed, MCP code overflow-wrap:anywhere) + regression test status_bar_wraps_instead_of_running_off_the_page. Counts lib 183/0, bin 81/0. Architecture chat's separate footer/wiki task (31.5.8/6.5.10/4.4.10) had NOT landed by 00:01 CST — no wiki-access change in v1.1.1; their worker warned it must rebase onto c5da01ee (status bar already fixed) to avoid a duplicate #status-bar edit.
# Independently verify 358 vs 370 (helios_stalled_parse)

Coordinate: 31.7.8/10.7.12/6.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-07 00:10 CST
Request (verbatim): see if you can independently verify which value is correct, and why the test is wrong
Status: complete — Will confirmed the Linux/Windows reading and directed handling both values; fix committed on provable-0.4.1, suite fully green (58/58)

Notes:
- Ground truth from raw bytes (Python scan, not the Rust parser): fixture blob (git object, 14,035 B, sha256 3a7c29bf…) has first 0x17 at offset 358; segment pure ASCII, 358 B = 358 chars. Fixture byte-identical at b5a8c5d and 84a8ae9. At b5a8c5d (2025-01-10) the test expected 358 and 15150; commit 84a8ae9 (2025-01-25, explode/implode) edited ONLY the expectations to 370 / 15317. Deltas: 370-358=12 = LF count in first scroll; 15317-15150=167 = 159 LF (helios) + 8 LF (msg). Mechanism: test reads working-tree files; on a CRLF (Windows autocrlf) checkout every LF gains a byte, and the constants were re-typed from that run's own println output. No .gitattributes pins fixture eol. Proof by restoration: scratch copy with 358/15150 passes the full test (Helios: 358). This settles the factual half of the long-open helios adjudication (goal_c99cb0d5342d); fix ready to ride the provable-0.4.1 PR as its own commit.
- FIX (Will, 2026-11-07 00:19: 'the tests pass on windows - we should probably just handle both values'): helios_stalled_parse now asserts 358||370 and 15150||15317 with the CRLF explanation inline; commit on branch provable-0.4.1 in ~/workspace/libphext-provable/libphext-rs; cargo test = 58 passed, 0 failed — first fully green run on Linux.
# Push phcc changes to GitHub (wbic16/phcc) and proceed

Coordinate: 31.7.9/8.6.9/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (from session record): push changes to phcc and proceed
Status: COMPLETE: wbic16/phcc main+exo @ 395f5d63; backup branch emise/pre-slice0-2026-11-07 @ 1b102067 preserved; fresh-clone ranch build ALL TESTS PASSED.

Results:
- wbic16/phcc main+exo @ 395f5d631ab8ee5659d7815adcb1f96237c40658; backup branch preserves old main 1b102067.
# qexo v1.0.3 forecast gate fix: forecast the node's configured lenses, not the legacy VM ceilings

Coordinate: 31.7.10/8.6.11/6.5.9
Issued: 2026-11-12 23:31 CST
Request (from session record): PR #10 (v1.0.2) replaced the disk gate with a volume lens + optional quota lens but left the forecast projecting the legacy absolute levels (byte AMBER 95 GB / RED 102 GB). Fleet evidence from the 2026-11-12 rollout: the second plan read on any ranch node flipped to FORECAST AMBER (95 GB projected in 0.0 days) over a GREEN gate. Fix: forecast crossings computed against the same configured lenses (volume free-fraction levels of the node's own volume; quota only when on, named as quota; file thresholds from config); legacy levels deleted from the forecast path; already-reached crossings belong to the gate, not projected at 0.0 d; projections bounded to a one-year horizon.
Status: MERGED 2026-11-12 (PR #12, merged_at 2026-11-13T05:39:19Z; exo head 1b819c2e). v1.0.3 forecast fix is on exo. Fleet nodes still run the v1.0.2 binary (gate-correct; forecast fix not yet rolled out — Will's call).

Results:
- Branch emise/forecast-gate-v1.0.3 @ 889da9b698a770440f5ece852a06c8a709dc29ad, parent 7bfc03cb (fresh at push), force disabled, remote tree verified 37/37 blobs+modes; diff vs v1.0.2 = 8 files.
- Gates (aletheia-core): cargo test 36/36 (33 + 3 new: ranch regression, filling-volume volume-RED, quota-named-quota); release build OK; wiring-check OK.
- Two-run CLI repro on the incident volume: run 2 stays GREEN, forecast reports no crossing — no FORECAST AMBER flip.
# Merge upstream into the exovim fork (release-0.12 line)

Coordinate: 31.7.10/9.7.11/7.6.9
Issued: 2026-11-09 22:25 CST
Request (verbatim): we need to merge upstream into our fork as well
Status: complete — upstream release-0.12 unchanged at pin; no merge existed to make

Notes:
- Interpretation (Emise, stated to Will): upstream for the exovim release line = neovim/neovim release-0.12, merged into exovim-0.12 (PR #2 updates in place). The master line was deliberately superseded (84c3a323) and is NOT re-merged; if release-0.12 has not moved past the pin a7ac6c466e, the agent reports that and the master delta for the record instead.
- DONE — NO-MERGE CASE (2026-11-09): upstream release-0.12 fetched fresh, head a7ac6c466e == the PATCHES.md pin, delta 0 commits; nothing merged, nothing pushed for this task. For the record: upstream master 0c4b90023dac stands 2,783 commits past the split point 2eb14c54; deliberately not merged per the supersede decision. Next check at the next release-0.12 movement (0.12.7 backports) or wave boundary.
# simple.phext — all of Will's tweets in Up Goer Five, holographically placed

Coordinate: 31.8.10/10.8.16/9.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-07 00:02 CST
Request (verbatim): let's build a special phext - one that translates all of my twitter posts from singular to up-goer-five - call it simple.phext. Place each tweet in the holographic coordinate it belongs to. Store the list of coordinates in timeline order. Make the archive easy to read and follow. Publish it to human.git as simple.phext.
Status: completed

Notes:
- simple.phext lives at wbic16/human@exo /simple.phext (Will directed it straight to human.git, outside the agi collection).
- Translation is deterministic from ~/workspace/simple-phext/ build scripts; numbers stay as digits because the UG5 list has no eight/nine/teens/tens words; frame scrolls (Home, indexes, map headers) are plain writing outside the UG5 gate, and Home says so.
- Honesty numbers: 86.6% of tokens carried with sense (kept / 1,439-entry map / stems); type carriers (thing, person, ...) carried 12.1%; 1.2% dropped (single letters, digit bits). 26.9% of tweets (7,936) needed no carrier and no drop. 351 wordless posts sit at the far corner 9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.9.
- 4,414 RT-prefixed posts in tweets.json are included as his posts.
- Coordinator verification (Emise, 2026-11-07 00:16): local SHA-256 09ff4e68...9eb385; parse count 29,582 non-empty; UG5 checker re-run clean; remote blob 0a72b2be... == local hash-object.

Results:
- 29,539 posts (2008-06-27 to 2025-06-16), each in Up Goer Five at its holographic coordinate; 29,582 scrolls total (43 frame: Home + 18 year indexes + map shelf).
- UG5 gate: zero flagged words over all tweet scrolls (before: 140,227 of 416,698 tokens outside the list).
- 3,730 posts bumped one or more scrolls for coordinate collisions; the year indexes record the true coordinates; every index line checked to land on a scroll with a matching date.
- Published: wbic16/human@exo commit 879a95cf; simple.phext 5,716,788 B. Build home: ~/workspace/simple-phext/ (BUILD-REPORT.md, MAP.md, scripts).
