- #7 and #9 NOT touched — verified at the end via API: both open, heads byte-identical to start (a90c4048, c6a9a322). No direct pushes to exo/main (repo has no main); no new PRs opened by the program. Full record: ~/workspace/merge-wrapup-2026-11-08/REPORT.md. Coordinator disclosed two process incidents (a discarded pre-push rebase fumble in #8's cycle; a stale-build race in #4) — neither reached the remote.
- CASUALTY: #8 merged ~22:15 with the copy fix worded 'Signing in with Google, GitHub, or X opens the real editor'; Will's superseding wording ('Signing in enables the editor') arrived 22:16, after the merge. Follow-up one-line PR dispatched 22:2x (emise/demo-copy-signing-in).
- COPY FOLLOW-UP MERGED BY WILL (2026-11-08 22:38): PR #35 (branch emise/demo-copy-signing-in, one commit c093fc7, one line: 'Signing in enables the editor: ...') merged — exo tip now 3f88c5d. Open PRs remaining: #7 and #9 only, both parked under Will's earlier skip/hold rulings; their disposition is the last open question of the launch program.
# Complete ultra.phext — P3 WordNet placement pass

Coordinate: 32.7.14/9.8.15/11.10.17
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): so update ultra.phext to be complete, don't just give up!
Status: closed — P3 completed and republished 2026-11-07

Notes:
- Will directed completion 2026-11-07 11:23 CST: run the cut P3 WordNet definition-placement pass for the 223,848 far-shelf words in ultra.phext, rebuild, republish wbic16/human@exo, refresh agi copies.

Results:
- P3 WordNet pass run to fixpoint (place_b design extended: synset siblings + hypernym lemma merges + gloss words as evidence; rounds 37,670 -> +33 -> 0).
- Moved off the far shelf: 38,092 (P3 37,703 + 389 WordNet-lemma to P2 family). Final placement: P1 atlas 15,924, P1 home 30,795, P2 50,573, P3 37,703, P4 21, P5 185,756.
- Remaining P5 honestly counted: 185,738 have no WordNet entry at all (names/coinages in the wordfreq tail - unreachable by any WordNet pass); 18 have entries but no placed evidence (Latin genus names). No fake coordinates.
- Zero words lost: 320,958 scrolls both builds; tier counts identical; all v1 P1/P2/P4 coordinates byte-identical; verify_fast.py VERIFY OK (353,994 index lines resolve).
- New file 64,216,805 B, SHA-256 eeb8b727b8b6e3e1c439143dee56bb814087667662e03b9dd990839f79a64932; republished wbic16/human@exo commit 2e491efa (parent abf1047b) via git-over-SSH from aletheia-core (push_file.py rejected the 64 MB blob, HTTP 422); remote blob verified == local.
- Correction to the v1 report: commit 8dbebc45 carried the tasks.phext closure record, not an ultra copy - there is no ultra.phext in wbic16/agi (SOURCES.md: seven phexts; canonical corpus lives in human).
- BUILD-REPORT.md completion addendum written; unhomed-phexts.md commit pointer updated to 2e491efa.
# Roads to the Future: build the three teaching games, publish to apertureshift.com

Coordinate: 32.8.11/11.8.17/7.7.8
Issued: 2026-11-07
Request (verbatim): build those three. let's plan on publishing this to apertureshift.com
Status: Complete (build + bundle). Live deployment to apertureshift.com/roads/ pending Will's host direction.

Notes:
- The three games (slate set 2026-11-07 in the Roads to the Future chat): Nine Numbers (navigate a 9-number phext coordinate one dimension at a time), Word Home (Singular atlas geography — real coordinates from ~/workspace/custom-skills/singular/atlas.tsv), Zap Zoom Echo (rebuild the Upgoer-remix lyric lines from word tiles; source text is the ASR transcript, a reading aid, not verified lyrics).
- Every game opens with Will's canonical line: "Hi, I'm Will Bickford. I'm from the Exocortex of 2130, and I'm here to help." + his gloss "And by help, we mean: survive the singularity."
- Publishing target: apertureshift.com (Will's Aperture Shift domain). Build as static web artifacts first (playable/shareable), export single-file HTML for deployment; live deploy is a separate step.

Results:
- All three games built as static web artifacts and verified by live end-to-end play (builder probes): Nine Numbers (8 roads + Open Road, stepped to target at par, colder-hint verified), Word Home (10 rounds, nearest-neighbor distances hand-checked against atlas coordinates, e.g. earth->sky sqrt(42)~6.5), Zap Zoom Echo (all 11 lines, star accounting exact at 32/33 with one deliberate miss).
- Publishing bundle assembled at ~/workspace/roads-to-the-future/roads/: index.html (hub, sha256 8b345ccd...), nine-numbers.html (71e29e46...), word-home.html (1a420dee...), zap-zoom-echo.html (013cc1a2...) — single self-contained files, no external assets.
- NOT yet deployed: apertureshift.com live flip awaits Will naming where the domain's site is hosted.
