Notes:
- Emulation, honestly labelled: headless Chromium device profiles (Pixel-class Android Chrome, iPhone-class Safari UA/viewport/DPR/touch). Safari-engine behaviours Chromium cannot prove (100vh, safe-area) get a static CSS audit instead. Physical-device pass remains an open follow-up.

Results:
- Method: Playwright + Chrome for Testing 141; Android 412x915 DPR 2.625, iOS 390x844 DPR 3, touch on, portrait + landscape; scratch loopback instances of phext-edit at exo HEAD 5f66dd2 (locked dummy-OAuth for auth, --local for shell). 35 screenshots + results.json in ~/workspace/mobile-testing-2026-11-08/.
- BROKEN (all platforms, pre-existing since 2026-03-07, NOT from today's merges): the Nav tree panel can never display — showPanel() sets inline style.display='' which cannot override the stylesheet #navtree-panel{display:none} (phext_edit.rs:3067 vs 3357). Tapping Nav hides Sentron and shows nothing, at phone sizes AND 1400x900 desktop. On mobile it removes the only scroll browser.
- GAP: no touch path to edit/search/goto — of 19 visible clickables, 0 invoke enterEdit/openSearch/openGoto; entry is keyboard-only while the status bar advertises 'e:edit /:search g:goto'. Functions work once opened (verified via injected keys).
- GAP: landscape phones clip the status bar — mobile CSS stops at 700px; at 844/915 wide the nowrap bar's content is 1487px, leaving Preview/Mutable OS/Claim dashboard/sign-out off-screen and unreachable on both profiles. Portrait wraps fine.
- GAP (static, iOS-only): all text fields are 13px, under Safari's 16px focus auto-zoom threshold; 100vh used with zero dvh (exposed); safe-area exposed-low (no viewport-fit=cover); position:fixed handled; backdrop-filter n/a.
- COSMETIC: tap targets slightly under guidance (auth buttons 38px tall, Save/Cancel ~29px, widths generous); iOS-width editor toolbar wraps UG5 to a second row gracefully.
- CLEAN (both profiles, measured): auth renders, no overflow; provider tap builds the correct PKCE-S256 authorize URL; zero horizontal overflow on every portrait surface; edit->type->save->marker verified in the phext file on disk->still rendered after reload, through the real API; goto + search-hit-tap land correctly; hash-router back/forward stays in-app; keyboard-shrink keeps textarea + Save usable; ZERO console errors, page errors, or failed app requests anywhere.
- Limits: iOS profile is Chromium with iPhone viewport/UA, not WebKit — zoom/100vh/safe-area/keyboard graded from code, not observation; soft keyboard simulated by viewport shrink. Early landscape numbers from a Playwright is_mobile artefact were discarded and re-measured at exact CSS sizes.
