Coordinate: 33.8.7/11.8.13/7.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-12 18:09 CST (evening commute voice call)
Request (from session record): Will's rule (2026-11-12): whenever we merge changes to SQ or any Rust-based tooling, queue a task to keep track of the next release needing to be scheduled — not necessarily deploy every change, but schedule a build and do not forget about producing builds. Trigger here: SQ PR #3 (seed cache + cache-aware fetch) merged 2026-11-12 18:08 CST at Will's direction (merge commit 7b94bafa).
Status: open — next SQ release build to be scheduled; batch further merged changes into it; build on a ranch node; this task closes when a release build from post-seed-cache exo exists and is verified. Also batched 2026-11-13: SQ PR #4 (libphext 0.6.0 + chain-aware hosting) merged by Will (merge commit 22b5f447). Publish probe 2026-11-13 (Will directed Emise to try from aletheia-core): credential present on the node, /source/SQ fast-forwarded to the merged exo, tests 77 green — but sq 0.5.6 is already on crates.io and the registry max is 0.6.0 (published 2026-10-27); publishing needs a version bump above 0.6.0, Will's call. Bump opened as SQ PR #5 (0.6.0 → 0.6.1) at Will's bump-to-v0.6 direction, register #99. PR #5 merged by Will 2026-11-13 (exo c4d5b19); sq 0.6.1 PUBLISHED from aletheia-core and verified live on crates.io (API max_version 0.6.1, updated 22:51:04Z). Register #99 resolved.
# qexo v1.0.1 doctor Windows fix: per-platform permissions and lock liveness

Coordinate: 33.8.8/8.8.11/9.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-12 22:48 CST
Request (from session record): Will merged PR #8 (qexo v1.0) and reported one Windows failure: doctor::tests::fix_repairs_dir_perms_and_stale_lock. Fix on a branch + PR, merges are Will's. Diagnosis: (1) the keyring check/test encoded unix permission modes as universal — mode_of is None and set_mode a no-op off-unix, yet the test asserted a repair to Some(0o700), and fix() would even claim the repair on Windows; (2) REAL BUG: stale_lock judged liveness by /proc/{pid}, which never exists on Windows, so a live process's lock would be judged stale and doctor --fix would delete it.
Status: PR-open awaiting Will's merge — PR #9 (emise/doctor-windows-v1.0.1 @ 3377d84b, parented on exo 970c6308). On merge, batches into release-build task 40.7.5/8.7.11/6.8.13.

Notes:
- Fix: pid_alive per platform (unix /proc unchanged; windows kernel32 FFI OpenProcess/GetExitCodeProcess, STILL_ACTIVE 259, null handle = dead only on ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER, all ambiguity reads alive; other platforms unjudgeable = alive). Keyring finding on non-unix is present-and-ok with 'permission modes are a unix concept, not applicable on this platform'; fix() only repairs/claims where a mode exists. Test restructured in place (same name): neutral segments everywhere, mode segment cfg(unix), not-applicable assertion cfg(not(unix)). Version 1.0.1 / v1.0.1 incl. plan::PLAN_VERSION stamp (the pattern exists in the scratch line).

Results:
- Gates on aletheia-core (cargo 1.94.0): baseline 29/29; after fix cargo test 29/29 (both doctor tests pass by name); release build OK; wiring-check OK (12 modules). cargo check --tests PASSES for x86_64-pc-windows-gnu AND x86_64-pc-windows-msvc (9 warnings, all pre-existing dead-code class). Battery spot re-run: seeded gnupg 755 + stale lock 999999 -> doctor exit 1 with both fixable -> --fix sets 700 + removes lock -> doctor exit 0; bare qexo human plan intact. Push verified 37/37 blobs+modes; diff vs exo exactly 9 files +149/-22. Windows runtime execution verified by Will's machine, not the ranch — stated in PR.
