Notes:
- Will merged PR #40 (flame favicon + optimized banner/background) and directed the deploy. Known risk: deploy.sh on awsbox may stop at a sudo step (wbic16 has no passwordless sudo there); if it does, the exact command needed comes back to Will. This deploy also covers register #51's outstanding deploy+robots.txt verification.
- Deploy attempt 2026-11-09 ~19:58 CST: merge ac80d589 confirmed on exo; /source/phext-lattice fast-forwarded 9458cb10 -> ac80d589 (clean). deploy.sh stops at 'sudo: a password is required' before building anything — wbic16 has password-gated sudo but a key-only SSH session cannot answer. Nothing built/installed/restarted; service untouched. Live site still serves the old assets (verified by hash). Unblock: interactive awsbox session, cd /source/phext-lattice && bash deploy/deploy.sh (as wbic16 or ubuntu).

Results:
- Live verification 2026-11-09 ~20:16 CST: favicon.ico 4,313 B ed6c1b73…, favicon.svg 858 B 584ee103…, banner.webp 182,496 B 6495d5fc…, background.webp 54,894 B, robots.txt has Allow: /?demo. The deploy ran between the 19:58 check (old build) and the 20:13 tick's fetch (new markers) — outside Emise's sessions. Register #51 closed; register now 18 active; todo.phext mirror rebuilt CURRENT (sha256 dd2bb44c…) and republish dispatched via aletheia-core.
