# qexo: internalize OpenPGP — no system-level gpg dependency (Android requirement)

Coordinate: 34.7.8/8.6.9/5.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-14 01:49 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 01:49 CST): 'qexo on android needs to not depend upon a system-level gpg — it should handle that internally.' Today qexo's crypto shells out to a system `gpg` binary for everything: node key generation, detached signing of release manifests and receipts, verification, armored public-key export, fingerprint/uid extraction. On Android that means the Termux gnupg package (port PR #1 route) or bundling a gpg into the APK (the main-chat APK build's hard part). Requirement: qexo performs OpenPGP in-process — an internal Rust implementation in the crypto layer, no external gpg binary on ANY platform (the fleet benefits too: one less system dependency everywhere). Keyring stays where it lives (state dir gnupg-format keys must remain readable, or keys are re-born under Will's direction — do NOT silently strand existing fleet keys; interop is the gate: internally produced keys and signatures must verify under the fleet's GnuPG, and fleet GnuPG signatures must verify internally — foreign-implementation conformance, the parser lesson applied to crypto). Delivery (Will, 2026-11-14 01:50 CST): rolled into wbic16/qexo as the next PR after Will merges PR #1 there.
Status: complete 2026-11-14

Notes:
- Sync rule (Will, 2026-11-14 02:08 CST; task 29.6.7/6.5.7/6.5.8): the internal-GPG change lands in quarterexo AND wbic16/qexo — the two repos stay synced; the Android PR carrying it also closes the recorded sync debt (parser + v1.4.x) unless staged separately at build time.
- DELIVERED 2026-11-14 (Phase A): quarterexo PR #22 (emise/internal-pgp-v1.6.0 @ 03741f1c, parented on exo ec2974d2) — FOR WILL'S REVIEW, register #105. Implementation: the pgp crate (rpgp 0.21.1) in-process replaces the gpg subprocess entirely (keygen, detached sign/verify, armored export, fingerprint/uid); pure Rust, Android-link-clean. NO STRANDED KEYS: GnuPG-era keyrings migrate transparently on first use into qexo-keys/ inside the same gnupg dir — the secret-key packet is rebuilt around GnuPG's own public-key bytes, fingerprint unchanged by construction; originals never modified (a rolled-back pre-1.6 binary still works); protected keys refused by name, generate will not re-key over them. FIND during the real-signer proof: KBX interleaves GnuPG trust packets that stop a parser binding the uid/self-signature — the migrated export came out as a bare key gpg refuses ('no user ID'); fixed by dropping trust packets on the way in (as gpg does on export) + a unit assertion that the uid survives migration. Gates (aletheia-core): cargo test 88/88; battery 16/16; interop 11/11 — (1) internal sign -> gpg VALIDSIG, (2) GnuPG-signed manifest accepted by internal verify + 1-byte mutation refused, (3) internal key imports into gpg with same fingerprint, (4) birth/register/sign/update --check with gpg absent from PATH; real-signer sandbox proof 7/7 (copy of live /var/lib/qexo migrated; internal release signature VALIDSIG A4E7277FB3EB0E589604BE5B506DBE3FC209E755 under system gpg; live state SHA-256 unchanged); census identical 15/830/2; windows-gnu LINK qexo.exe sha256 9e060fdd...; Android LINK sha256 2578786c.... Status: awaiting Will's review/merge of PR #22; publish + fleet rollout follow his word and batch into release task 40.7.5/8.7.11/6.8.13. Phase B carried this into wbic16/qexo PR #2 (see 29.6.7/6.5.7/6.5.8).
- 2026-11-14 03:37 CST: Will reported merge conflicts on quarterexo PR #22. Verified: sole conflict was Cargo.lock (one hunk — the v1.5.0 lock-sync on exo vs the branch's 1.6.0 stamp line). Repaired under the standing rebase rule: impact check clean (single Emise commit; only open PR; nothing based on it), backup branch backup/internal-pgp-v1.6.0-pre-rebase-2026-11-14 preserved at 03741f1c, rebased onto exo 81254808, force-with-lease push anchored at the old tip; new head 93ca206b6678b0cb4407320154beae692e2af892. API: mergeable=true, clean. Gates re-run on the rebased tree (aletheia-core): cargo test 88/88, lock clean after cargo run, battery green, census identical 15/830/2, windows-gnu LINK, Android LINK byte-identical to pre-rebase build (2578786c…), interop 11/11. PR #22 open for Will's merge (#105).

Results:
- quarterexo PR #22: https://github.com/wbic16/quarterexo/pull/22 @ 03741f1c — v1.6.0 internal OpenPGP (rpgp), all gates green incl. real-signer migration proof; awaiting Will's merge
