- LANDED + VERIFIED (worker report ~/workspace/phext-notepad-perf/REPORT-ULTRA-OPEN.md; Emise verified remote branch emise/ultra-open-fix @ 2c75b8dfefb35b5c212883a8815e702d8e38f05d via API): DIAGNOSIS (measured headless with the real app code): (1) DATA LOSS, the headline — WinForms Coordinates are short-backed; ultra's components reach 223,854, so the old load held only 162,640 of 320,958 scrolls (54,550 at wrapped negative coordinates, only 23% intact) and Serialize() would have written back 24.0M of 35.3M chars — saving after the hang would have destroyed ~2/3 of ultra.phext. The published copy in wbic16/human@exo is untouched (SHA-256 fd68c5b0... verified at build time). (2) Load built 4,470,631 TreeNode allocations + a 1,652,158-entry name->node cache keyed over the TRAVERSED coordinate space (incl. empty groups), then ExpandAll, all on the UI thread: 3.04 GB managed churn measured — matches Will's 2,024,408 K screenshot; cost tracked coordinate-space churn, not file size (0.7 MB singular took 2.7 s). (3) Recursive getter chain in PhextText (~27.8 us/scroll via 36 dictionary walks per get, twice per setScroll) over a raw parse walk of only 64 ms. The brief's quadratic-vendored-explode hypothesis was NOT confirmed — the WinForms tokenizer is already single-pass. FIX: Coordinates short->int; model made WinForms-free (TreeNode/Cache/Get*TreeRoot removed — dictionary effects proven no-ops by the dumps); accessors iterative; new WinForms-free PhextTree (child enumeration, find-as-path, subtree walks); form materializes 130 root nodes at open (vs 379,099 eager), populates on BeforeExpand, parse on a background thread behind a re-entrancy guard. RESULTS (measured, same harness): ultra load 32-40 s -> 0.52-0.71 s; allocated 3.04 GB -> 247 MB; setScroll 27.8 -> 3.7 us; scrolls held 162,640 -> 320,958 (all). agi 2.7 s -> 79 ms. 43/43 headless checks: agi/singular/CYOA enumeration+Serialize+checksum BYTE-IDENTICAL to the old implementation; ultra enumeration matches an independent Python ground truth exactly; lazy walk reproduces all 379,099 eager nodes with matching names/child counts. Real-WinForms figures in the report are ESTIMATES (~300-400 MB, ~1 s) awaiting Will's build. NATIVE APP: no perf disease on ultra (580 ms, 86 MB measured) but a dependency one — it still sits on libphext 0.3.1 whose COORDINATE_MAXIMUM=1000 collapses ultra to 41,963/320,958 scrolls; reported, NOT fixed (libphext freeze; widening the native app's coordinate source is Will's call). Two documented catches: 9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.9 is a REAL ultra scroll ('floatable'), not an absence probe; deleteNode's pre-existing Contains('-') guard makes it unreachable — preserved verbatim, flagged.
