# qexo disk gate is a VM instrument: gate on free space and volume fraction, thresholds in state.phext config

Coordinate: 36.6.8/8.6.11/6.6.10
Issued: 2026-11-12 22:51 CST
Request (from session record): Will ran qexo on aletheia-core (2026-11-12) and the disk gate read RED at 809 GB used on a 3.6 TB volume with 2.7 TB free (df: 754 GiB used, 22%). Cause: the gate's absolute thresholds (AMBER 95 GB / RED 102 GB used; files 1.1M/1.3M) were calibrated to the Muse VM's staging quota in the v2 planner and ported value-for-value ever since; the probe measures used bytes on whatever volume the config root sits on, so the VM instrument condemns any real node. Fix: gate on free space + used fraction of the measured volume, report total/free in the plan (units consistent), thresholds read from the config homeland (9.9.9/9.9.9/9.9.9) in state.phext with sane defaults, and gate copy that names the actual volume instead of 'the VM'. Sequencing: dispatch the moment the v1.0.1 doctor-Windows slice lands — both slices touch Cargo/VERSION/CHANGELOG.
Status: MERGED 2026-11-12 (PR #11, merged_at 2026-11-13T05:34:38Z, after PR #10 had landed on its stacked base; carried to exo by PR #11). exo carries v1.0.2.
