Status: Complete: 4 of 5 files refreshed (Makefile, PATCHES.md, libtcc.c, tcc.h); lib/libtcc1.c HELD at pre-F1 bytes — all bindings (WP/CBMC/differential receipts + both listings) name the pre-F1 hash 0e2eb64b, receipts stay CURRENT. Final phext 54ab8532, seal 95562b0c, gate v8.1.0 verdict Sec 20. Carried tree 557/558 = repo, make test ALL PASSED (aletheia-core). Extra finding: Sec-14 addendum phext.c/h still pre-F4. Not pushed. HOLD CLOSED 2026-11-07 by the F1 receipt re-issue (~/workspace/phcc-reissue/): libtcc1.c now carried at F1 bytes 69879e2a; WP/CBMC/differential receipts re-issued at their coordinates with honestly re-run evidence — WP reproduced 271/297 exactly per function (152/168, 32/33, 29/29, 9/9, 8/8, 13/16, 14/17, 14/18; same 26 timeout opens), CBMC 5/5, differential 94 defined/34 undefined/0 divergences, artifact-equivalence 7,242,324 comparisons 0 divergences. Sec-14 addendum refreshed to F4 bytes in the same pass. Final re-issued phext 82bd0745 (63,195,664 B), seal ffadce9b; gate v8.1.0 all CURRENT (listings 3/3, STALE 0, conformance 328/333 / MSVC NOT ATTESTED); unpack 558/558 byte-identical to e399b212 incl. libtcc1.c; make test ALL PASSED. Not pushed.
# Bring phext-notepad (emise/ultra-open-fix) up to libphext v0.5.0 parity

Coordinate: 36.12.9/14.14.18/13.11.15
Issued: 2026-11-08 16:42 CST
Request (verbatim): in that same branch, also bring it up to libphext v0.5.0 parity
Status: COMPLETE 2026-11-08 — commit 636989e on emise/ultra-open-fix pushed + API-verified; report inscribed in artifacts.phext

Notes:
- Same branch as the ultra-open fix: wbic16/phext-notepad emise/ultra-open-fix @ 2c75b8df (task 34.7.10/8.7.12/8.8.13). Add parity work ON TOP of that branch; do not fork a new branch.
- Open item it closes: the native app still sits on libphext 0.3.1 semantics — COORDINATE_MAXIMUM=1000 collapses ultra.phext to 41,963/320,958 scrolls there. v0.5.0 parity means: unbounded coordinates (0.4), linear tokenize (already in the app's own parser — verify), binary scrolls + xz seal (0.5), with cross-checks against the libphext-rs 0.5.0 reference implementation and fixtures.
- Will's follow-up question answered 2026-11-08: publishing libphext-cs 0.5.0 to NuGet is NOT a prerequisite for this work — phext-notepad does not consume libphext-cs (WinForms vendors its own C# phext sources; the native app is Rust). The cs 0.5.0 pack/push remains Will's separate outstanding publish act for NuGet consumers (two packages: libphext-cs + Phext.Seal).

Results:
