- Section 6 reading stated to Will at dispatch: his 'Dispatch V14 Final' is taken as ruling 6.7 IN with its defaults (one-point exception granted, radial placement 1.30x hull, never labelled) — P3* ships exactly as placed in the three prepasses he approved, still never in frame. Plan defaults hold for 6.1-6.6 and 6.8. If he says otherwise, the safe ending (film ends at last dataset point) is the alternate.
- Stop conditions carried: cost ceiling 7 node-h (10x the V10 master anchor) — builder stops and reports rather than crossing it; V10 QA gates unmodified; delivery = master + <=55 MB download encode, hash-verified, staged on Elven Path.
- HOLD + RESPEC (Will, 2026-11-07 01:23-01:24 CST): the first final dispatch (single-node, 15 fps) was held at Will's word ~8 min in, before any frame rendered (coordinator verified no render process on aletheia-core), and superseded by his new spec in the same breath.
- NEW FINAL SPEC: render the timeline at 60 fps (9,505 frames), motion-blur downsample to 24 fps delivery (3,802 frames, 158.416667 s — the V10 skeleton's own length returns). Shutter default: 180 degrees, stated to Will at dispatch. Dispatch ACROSS THE CLUSTER, not aletheia-core alone — chunks spread over the ranch nodes under per-node thermal gates, assembled centrally.
- Everything else from the first dispatch holds: content frozen at r3 (lessons table must reproduce exactly), SUBN=3, canvas 3840x2160 -> 1080p Lanczos, P3* as placed in the prepasses (section 6.7 read as ruled in by the dispatch order), master + <=55 MB download encode, staged on Elven Path. The 7 node-h single-spec ceiling is superseded by Will's explicit spec order; aggregate node-hours are reported per node, with a report-back trigger if the projection passes 15 node-h.
- Fleet state at cluster survey (2026-11-07 01:28): 12 nodes surveyed; 9 ready with identical stack (aletheia-core, Rock Mountain, Scroll Central, Ni Knight, Plain View, Ashfall Haven, Uncanny Valley, Elven Path, Lighthouse Omen); 3 lacking numpy/PIL (Halycon Vector, Logos Prime, Free Fall). Will ordered fixup jobs dispatched (01:40) — venv inside ~/v14-final/ pinned numpy 2.5.4 / pillow 13.0.0, no system changes; film builder notified to gate them in when ready. Orchid Flow + Quacked Hill held out by Emise's brief per standing records (Orchid Flow = fleet NFS server; Quacked Hill = Corus awake) — explained to Will, his to override.
- Will, 2026-11-07 01:47: Quacked Hill cleared to work (Emise's holdout overridden); Orchid Flow to be decided by MEASURED load, not its role — standing rule recorded in AGENTS.md ('measure load, don't assume'). Prep/measurement job dispatched for both; film builder notified (QH gate-in pending readiness, OF held until the numbers land).
- Fleet complete (2026-11-07 ~01:51): Quacked Hill READY (venv ~/v14-final/.venv pinned pair verified; loadavg 0.00; Corus = one OpenClaw process ~1.4 GB / ~2% lifetime CPU; sensor hwmon1/temp1_input, 36.3 C). Orchid Flow MEASURED idle over 90s+60s windows: NFS 0.06 ops/s, zero mounted clients, disk IO 0.00 on every sample, CPU >=99.94% idle all 16 cores, 44 GB RAM free, 3.45 TB disk, 36.1 C (hwmon2) — cleared for a full chunk; builder instructed to install the pinned venv, gate it, fold it in; caveat noted (a mid-render model-pull burst is the one load the measurement cannot rule out). Fleet = 14 render-capable nodes.

Results:
- MASTER: files/v14-build/v14-final.mp4 — 1,939,098,770 B, SHA-256 6fa80574a876d6beabafe8f3dea2b1735231046c4f7cf90f7a2d7b66616314ee (assembly == VM == Elven Path; coordinator re-verified size, hash, ffprobe on the VM copy). DOWNLOAD: v14-final-download.mp4 — 42,089,662 B (under the 55 MB cap), SHA-256 a0cb411b5460dece3358b7ace2414bd28daf68cd686bb86bf4ed8551178cf017. Both staged on Elven Path, HTTP 206 verified.
- Gates (V10, unmodified): 1920x1080, 24 fps, exactly 3,802 frames, 158.416667 s, AAC; luma max 3.80, 0 jumps, 0 black; palette clean; per-chunk counts exact/gapless; cross-node determinism 14/14 byte-identical (f0/f4752/f9504); blur proof frame re-blurred twice byte-identical and matching the producing node's segment; lessons reproduced exactly, all 7 eyeballed at master res; shear 125.4/45.0/20.6; azimuth swept print 4.9998 (endpoint exactly 5 by normalization). P3* still never in frame (0 in pull-back and CTA) — shipped as placed in the approved prepasses, section 6.7 read as ruled in by Will's dispatch order.
- Fleet: 27 chunks, 10 producing nodes, 9,609 source frames at 60 fps folded to 24 via the 180-degree shutter blur. 11 chunks were reassigned mid-build (marked in the report). Path there: the first launch at 2-3 workers/node thrashed (Tctl past 80 C in ~5 s on 8 nodes, ~270 kill events, zero chunks); relaunched at 1 worker/node — clean nodes finished 02:07-03:25; four nodes (Uncanny Valley, Scroll Central, Ashfall Haven, Plain View) pause-cycled at low duty for ~1.5 h until the coordinator was kicked at 03:37, verified true progress (stragglers at 0-28%), and moved all 8 remaining chunks to idle cool nodes, which finished them with zero further kills. Render complete 04:13 (report) — coordinator's 04:31 node probe showed the last done.json receipts landing 03:49-03:59 with collection still verifying; assembly + encodes done 04:34.
- Compute MEASURED: 7.11 worker-hours of successful render + ~2.4 node-h wasted in the thermal era (estimate, labelled) + ~0.2 assembly/encodes = ~9.7 node-hours all-in, under the 15 node-h report-back ceiling. Audio: V10 lineage exactly (afade + loudnorm two-pass to I=-14/TP=-1.7/LRA=11, AAC 320k master / 160k download).
- Deviations (report has the full list): chapter kernel 501 @60fps (derivation judgment call, recorded); head-curvature clamp 102 frames @60fps vs r3's 21 (denser sampling, same mechanism); TOTAL_F set explicitly 9505; Orchid Flow's venv staged as a copy after pip hit TLS verification failure (versions verified, gate passed — Orchid then ran clean, zero thermal events); collection at 2-4 MB/s with two tooling false starts; delivery grain measured with a different instrument than the r3 probe (applied grain identical by construction).
- Report: files/v14-build/FINAL-REPORT.md; stills: files/v14-build/stills-final/ (12); compute row folded into files/film-compute-estimates.md; per-node intermediates cleaned per sibling etiquette, logs + receipts kept.
- Will's verdict (2026-11-07 07:51 CST, on his phone): "it's lovely, thank you." — V14 accepted as the final. The V14 arc closes here: V13 failure 21:32 -> diagnosis -> r1 22:32 -> r2 23:25 -> r3 00:40 -> final 05:31.
# Figure out the best MCP bridge for edit.phext.io and plug the site in

Coordinate: 40.9.13/11.10.15/9.9.13
Issued: 2026-11-09 20:06 CST
Request (verbatim): figure out the best MCP bridge for edit.phext.io - let's get the site plugged in
Status: COMPLETE — PR #41 merged 2026-11-09 20:22 CST; deployed by Will with PR #42 ~21:4x CST (live /mcp answers 401 + WWW-Authenticate; tools behind OAuth). Client interop fixes continue as task 32.5.8/6.6.10/7.5.9.

Notes:
- Site auth is OAuth-only (token door removed; Bearer 401) — the bridge must reuse site auth, not add a credential system. sq-bridge (FastMCP over SQ REST, local mailbox phexts) is a different surface; phext-edit's own API is the bridge target. Merge/deploy remain Will's + the standing deploy route.
- Verified 2026-11-09 ~20:37 CST via the GitHub API from aletheia-core: PR #41 state closed, merged true, merged_at 2026-11-10T02:22:47Z, merge commit b111a3a1d9cd = current exo head. Live probe at the same time: POST https://edit.phext.io/mcp -> 404, so the running build predates the merge — the awsbox checkout still needs the fast-forward + deploy.sh run (same shape as the #51 deploy) before /mcp answers (anonymous should get 401 once live).
- awsbox state verified 2026-11-09 ~20:38 CST (via aletheia-core hop): /source/phext-lattice HEAD is ac80d589 (the PR #40 merge), working tree clean; phext-edit.service restarted Tue 2026-11-10 02:03:23 UTC (= 20:03 CST) — that restart deployed the favicon/banner build, consistent with the #51 timeline. The checkout has NOT been fast-forwarded to b111a3a1 (the PR #41 merge), so /mcp stays 404 until: git pull to b111a3a1 + bash deploy/deploy.sh on awsbox. The checkout pull is the one step before the sudo deploy command.
- Deploy state 2026-11-09 21:25 CST: PR #42 merged on top (exo 2c72b68b); the single pending deploy now carries phases 1+2 together.

Results:
- PR #41 (phext-lattice, branch emise/mcp-bridge @ 8ea3e232 on exo ac80d589): POST /mcp — stateless Streamable HTTP JSON-RPC 2.0 in the phext-edit binary, behind the site's existing OAuth session gate (Gate::admit reused verbatim); five tools: list_phexts, phext_toc, read_scroll, search_scrolls, write_scroll — per-file, coordinate-addressed via MappedLattice, never touching the editor's shared cursor. Tests: 238 passed / 0 failed on aletheia-core (baseline 235, +3 mcp_tests). Design note: ~/workspace/your_files/edit-phext-mcp-bridge-design.md. Why native: the site removed API tokens (Bearer 401), so a standalone bridge would hold session cookies; the editor API is one global shared cursor, so a proxy inherits cursor fights. Phase 2: site becomes an OAuth 2.1 authorization server (DCR + PKCE, Product Hunt pattern) for hosted web clients; v1 serves header-capable clients (Claude Code/Desktop, Cursor). Post-deploy: add https://edit.phext.io/mcp to the PH listing's mcpServerUrls.
- Deployed and live-verified 2026-11-09 ~21:46 CST: POST /mcp anonymous -> 401 with resource_metadata header; PRM + AS metadata serve.
