Coordinate: 42.7.8/7.7.10/7.7.12
Issued: 2026-11-12 23:41 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-12 23:41 CST), building exo@1b819c2 (v1.0.3) on Windows: 'unresolved external symbol statvfs'. Diagnosis: probe_disk in src/core.rs declared POSIX statvfs unconditionally; Windows has no such symbol, so the build failed at link time — invisible to the v1.0.1 gates, which ran cargo check (never links) for the Windows targets. Fix: volume_at() split per platform — statvfs on unix (semantics unchanged), GetDiskFreeSpaceExW on Windows mapped into the same Volume terms, None elsewhere; the gate set gains a full Windows link.
Status: MERGED 2026-11-12 by Will (PR #13; exo head 560e97e0). v1.0.4 on exo. PR #14 rebase onto it directed by Will the same evening.

Results:
- Gates (aletheia-core): cargo test 37/37 (36 baseline + win32 mapping test); release build OK; wiring-check OK; cargo check --tests PASS windows-gnu + windows-msvc; FULL LINK cargo build --target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu produced qexo.exe (PE32+, imports GetDiskFreeSpaceExW, no statvfs reference); unix battery: bare qexo on incident volume GREEN, 755 GiB of 3,663 GiB, matches df. Extern audit: statvfs was the only unconditional unix extern in src/. Record: ~/workspace/qexo-task/statvfsfix/BUILD-RECORD.md
# Paper 007 ingestion — Subquadratic Attention with a Hierarchical Tree-Structured Indexer (arXiv:2610.42112)

Coordinate: 44.2.2/2.2.5/2.2.11
Issued: 2026-11-07 23:54 CST
Request (verbatim): https://www.alphaxiv.org/pdf/2610.42112
Status: complete 2026-11-08

