# libphext-cs v0.5.0 SealTests fail on Windows — XZInit fix

Coordinate: 50.13.10/11.16.31/31.10.15
Issued: 2026-11-09
Request (verbatim): libphext-cs v0.5.0 is throwing this error on test
Status: complete — fix pushed and PR open; awaiting Will merge + Windows re-run

Notes:
- Screenshot (Will, 2026-11-09 22:55 CST, VS Test Explorer, Windows): 60 tests, 55 passed, 5 failed — all SealTests. Three show InvalidOperationException 'Please call XZInit.GlobalInit() first!' at XZStream..ctor via PhextSeal.SealBytes line 67; Test_SealRoundTripRealPhext shows PlatformNotSupportedException; Test_UnsealRejectsNonXzData fails Assert.Throws exact-type.
- Root cause verified from Joveler source (master, fetched 2026-11-09): Joveler.Compression.XZ XZLoader.DefaultLibFileName returns 'liblzma.so.5' on Linux and 'liblzma.dylib' on macOS, and throws PlatformNotSupportedException on Windows — so parameterless XZInit.GlobalInit() can never succeed on Windows; Joveler's USAGE.md says Windows callers must pass the explicit path runtimes/win-<arch>/native/liblzma.dll. PhextSeal.EnsureInitialized called the parameterless overload, so it worked only on the Linux ranch (system liblzma) and masked the bug in the 60/60 ranch run.
- Compounding bug in PhextSeal: EnsureInitialized latches _initialized=1 via Interlocked.Exchange BEFORE GlobalInit succeeds. On Windows the first Seal call throws the real PlatformNotSupportedException (absorbed by whichever test ran first — RealPhext in Will's run), and every later call skips init and dies with the misleading 'call GlobalInit first' message; Unseal's non-xz path then throws InvalidOperationException instead of InvalidDataException, breaking the Throws test.
- Fix written to PhextSeal.cs only: resolve bundled liblzma at runtimes/<rid>/native under AppContext.BaseDirectory (RID from ProcessArchitecture), flattened-beside-assembly fallback, parameterless system search only as Linux/macOS fallback, clear PlatformNotSupportedException naming the searched path on Windows; _initialized now latches only after GlobalInit succeeds, under a lock. Encoder options unchanged (preset 6, CRC64).

Results:
- Ranch verification (aletheia-core, fresh clone @ exo + fix): dotnet test 60/60 passed; test output contains runtimes/win-x64/native/liblzma.dll, the exact path the resolver passes on Windows; win-x64 publish flattens liblzma.dll beside the app (fallback path covers it).
- Branch emise/seal-windows-init-fix @ fbdeb27 (parent exo 27cb1a3) pushed from aletheia-core; PR #2 open https://github.com/wbic16/libphext-cs/pull/2 — remote PhextSeal.cs blob 1c54ad7a, SHA-256 e419484d098760cde4… identical to local.
- NuGet checked live 2026-11-09: Phext.Seal not yet published, libphext-cs only 0.3.0 — the fix lands inside 0.5.0 before Will publishes; no version bump. Remaining: Will merges PR #2, pulls, re-runs Test Explorer on Windows (the one surface the ranch cannot test).
