Coordinate: 53.14.8/18.8.27/6.9.10
Issued: 2026-11-14 01:43 CST
Request (from session record): Will (2026-11-14 01:43-01:44 CST): 'we need to source efficient benchmarks to measure our progress against' + 'so a benchmark view — similar to MOAT's progress bar — is warranted.' Efficient = small, fast, cheap, repeatable, runnable on our own cadence (the Anthropic pattern from the SOTA scan: ~20 real queries, run on every change — a benchmark that costs a day measures nothing twice). Coverage: (1) qexo mission metrics — intent-to-first-action latency, queue integrity (zero lost, audited), resume success under the 3-failure cap, bridge uptime; (2) the model line — TLM held-out next-letter top-1 (existing: trie 0.268, sliding 0.388), watts at human-real-time speed toward the 20W AGI target, plus public anchors small enough to run (LoCoMo-class memory evals, compact coding/reasoning subsets) chosen for cost-per-signal; every benchmark ships with its target so progress is a fraction, not a vibe. THE VIEW: `qexo bench` renders each benchmark in Will's MOAT bar form (standing rule, 2026-11-08): old block-bar look, colorized — green to the point estimate, yellow extending to the top of the range, white for the remainder — PRIOR and CURRENT side by side with the delta called out (improved / held / fell). Benchmark results are state records (phext) so the view is the same on phone, laptop, and fleet.
